1
00:00:54,785 --> 00:00:56,495
Now, I know what you're thinking.

2
00:00:56,662 --> 00:01:00,032
"Oh, no! Thor's in a cage.
How did this happen?"

3
00:01:00,207 --> 00:01:01,997
Well, sometimes you have to get captured

4
00:01:02,084 --> 00:01:03,884
just to get a straight answer
out of somebody.

5
00:01:05,212 --> 00:01:08,332
It's a long story,
but basically, I'm a bit of a hero.

6
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:12,100
See, I spent some time on Earth...

7
00:01:12,553 --> 00:01:15,633
Fought some robots,
saved the planet a couple of times.

8
00:01:15,931 --> 00:01:17,561
Then I went searching through the Cosmos

9
00:01:17,641 --> 00:01:20,561
for some magic,
colorful Infinity Stone things.

10
00:01:21,353 --> 00:01:23,853
Didn't find any.

11
00:01:24,023 --> 00:01:28,063
That's when I came across
a path of death and destruction,

12
00:01:28,235 --> 00:01:30,905
which led me all the way here
into this cage,

13
00:01:32,615 --> 00:01:33,905
where I met you.

14
00:01:39,997 --> 00:01:41,747
How much longer do you think
we'll be here?

15
00:01:55,805 --> 00:01:59,476
Thor, son of Odin.

16
00:02:00,018 --> 00:02:03,318
Surtur, son of a bitch.

17
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:04,570
You're still alive.

18
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:08,900
I thought my father killed you
a half a million years ago.

19
00:02:09,069 --> 00:02:10,699
I cannot die.

20
00:02:10,862 --> 00:02:12,622
Not until I fulfill my destiny

21
00:02:12,781 --> 00:02:15,041
and lay waste to your home.

22
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,700
It's funny you should mention that.

23
00:02:16,868 --> 00:02:19,158
Because I've been having these
terrible dreams of late.

24
00:02:19,329 --> 00:02:21,579
Asgard up in flames, falling to ruins.

25
00:02:21,748 --> 00:02:24,538
And you, Surtur,
are at the center of all of them.

26
00:02:24,709 --> 00:02:28,549
Then you have seen Ragnarok,
the fall of Asgard.

27
00:02:28,713 --> 00:02:30,583
- The great prophecy...
- Hang on.

28
00:02:31,007 --> 00:02:32,007
Hang on.

29
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:36,350
I'll be back around shortly.

30
00:02:36,513 --> 00:02:39,353
I really feel like
we were connecting there.

31
00:02:42,018 --> 00:02:45,228
Okay, so Ragnarok.
Tell me about that. Walk me through it.

32
00:02:45,397 --> 00:02:47,397
My time has come.

33
00:02:47,566 --> 00:02:50,696
When my crown is reunited
with the Eternal Flame,

34
00:02:50,861 --> 00:02:53,531
I shall be restored to my full might.

35
00:02:53,697 --> 00:02:55,947
I will tower over the mountains,

36
00:02:56,116 --> 00:02:58,696
and bury my sword deep in Asgard's...

37
00:02:58,869 --> 00:03:01,409
Hang on. Give it a second.

38
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:04,500
I swear, I'm not even moving.
It's just doing this on its own.

39
00:03:04,666 --> 00:03:06,246
I'm really sorry.

40
00:03:07,252 --> 00:03:08,882
Okay, so let me get this straight.

41
00:03:09,045 --> 00:03:12,675
You're going to put your crown
into the Eternal Flame

42
00:03:12,841 --> 00:03:15,221
and then you'll suddenly grow as big
as a house?

43
00:03:15,385 --> 00:03:16,545
A mountain!

44
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,770
The Eternal Flame that Odin keeps
locked away on Asgard?

45
00:03:19,931 --> 00:03:22,481
Odin is not on Asgard.

46
00:03:22,642 --> 00:03:26,562
And your absence has left the throne
defenseless.

47
00:03:26,730 --> 00:03:28,570
Okay, so where is it? This crown?

48
00:03:28,732 --> 00:03:31,782
This is my crown,
the source of my power.

49
00:03:32,152 --> 00:03:35,532
Oh, that's a crown.
I thought it was a big eyebrow.

50
00:03:35,697 --> 00:03:36,867
It's a crown.

51
00:03:37,032 --> 00:03:40,542
Anyway, it sounds like
all I have to do to stop Ragnarok

52
00:03:40,702 --> 00:03:42,502
is rip that thing off your head.

53
00:03:43,663 --> 00:03:46,283
But Ragnarok has already begun.

54
00:03:46,458 --> 00:03:48,378
You cannot stop it.

55
00:03:57,969 --> 00:04:01,059
I am Asgard's doom, and so are you.

56
00:04:01,223 --> 00:04:04,813
All will suffer, all will burn.

57
00:04:04,976 --> 00:04:06,686
That's intense.

58
00:04:06,853 --> 00:04:08,683
To be honest,
seeing you grow really big

59
00:04:08,856 --> 00:04:11,356
and set fire to a planet
would be quite the spectacle.

60
00:04:11,943 --> 00:04:14,203
But it looks like I'm gonna have to
choose option B,

61
00:04:14,362 --> 00:04:16,112
where I bust out of these chains,

62
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:20,160
knock that tiara off your head,
and stash it away in Asgard's vault.

63
00:04:20,326 --> 00:04:23,286
You cannot stop Ragnarok.

64
00:04:23,454 --> 00:04:24,704
Why fight it?

65
00:04:24,914 --> 00:04:28,374
Because that's what heroes do.

66
00:04:33,339 --> 00:04:35,429
Wait, I'm sorry.
I didn't time that right.

67
00:04:37,218 --> 00:04:38,678
And, now!

68
00:04:43,182 --> 00:04:46,852
You have made a grave mistake, Odinson.

69
00:04:47,019 --> 00:04:49,649
I make grave mistakes all the time.

70
00:04:51,399 --> 00:04:54,069
Everything seems to work out.

71
00:06:12,897 --> 00:06:16,607
Heimdall, I know it's been a while,
but I could really use a fast exit.

72
00:06:18,112 --> 00:06:19,532
Heimdall?

73
00:06:20,531 --> 00:06:22,411
Heimdall was an idiot.

74
00:06:22,574 --> 00:06:24,534
This job should have made him rich.

75
00:06:25,452 --> 00:06:26,952
Now, the job ain't easy

76
00:06:27,121 --> 00:06:29,041
but it does have its benefits.

77
00:06:29,206 --> 00:06:33,456
The Bifrost gives me access to
everything the Nine Realms has to offer.

78
00:06:33,627 --> 00:06:35,917
I mean, it's all mine for the taking.

79
00:06:37,339 --> 00:06:38,589
Behold...

80
00:06:40,759 --> 00:06:42,089
My stuff.

81
00:06:44,096 --> 00:06:45,926
I'm particularly fond of these.

82
00:06:46,098 --> 00:06:49,638
I pulled them out of a place on Midgard
called Texas.

83
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:52,850
I even named them. Des and Troy.

84
00:06:53,939 --> 00:06:56,069
You see, when you put them together,

85
00:06:57,067 --> 00:06:58,317
they destroy.

86
00:07:17,379 --> 00:07:19,299
Heimdall, come on.

87
00:07:39,443 --> 00:07:40,493
Stay!

88
00:07:42,237 --> 00:07:45,117
Heimdall?
I'm running short on options.

89
00:07:45,657 --> 00:07:46,987
Heimdall?

90
00:07:48,535 --> 00:07:49,535
Skurge?

91
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:54,170
Is that important?

92
00:08:01,131 --> 00:08:03,051
You girls are in for a treat.

93
00:08:56,146 --> 00:08:57,156
Girls!

94
00:08:58,982 --> 00:09:02,822
Well, well, well.
Look who decided to pop in.

95
00:09:02,986 --> 00:09:06,786
Thanks for scaring away my company
and drenching my workplace in brains.

96
00:09:06,948 --> 00:09:07,948
Who are you?

97
00:09:08,032 --> 00:09:11,202
Don't you remember? I'm Skurge.
We fought together on Vanaheim.

98
00:09:11,369 --> 00:09:13,619
Right. Where is Heimdall?

99
00:09:14,122 --> 00:09:16,792
That traitor. No one knows.
He's a fugitive of the throne.

100
00:09:17,333 --> 00:09:18,583
Traitor?

101
00:09:18,752 --> 00:09:21,342
Yeah. You see, Odin charged Heimdall
with negligence of duty

102
00:09:21,504 --> 00:09:23,424
but he disappeared before the trial.

103
00:09:23,590 --> 00:09:25,910
Hard to catch a guy who can see
everything in the universe.

104
00:09:25,967 --> 00:09:26,967
Sure.

105
00:09:27,051 --> 00:09:29,591
Hold on.
I'm supposed to announce your arrival.

106
00:09:53,578 --> 00:09:55,248
What the hell is that?

107
00:10:03,129 --> 00:10:05,959
Oh, brother. This is it.

108
00:10:06,132 --> 00:10:07,512
I take my leave.

109
00:10:08,259 --> 00:10:10,389
You fool, you didn't listen!

110
00:10:10,553 --> 00:10:11,603
I'm sorry.

111
00:10:11,763 --> 00:10:12,803
Lady Sif, get help!

112
00:10:12,972 --> 00:10:14,102
Somebody, help!

113
00:10:14,891 --> 00:10:16,311
Sorry for all I've done.

114
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:18,230
It's all right. Hold on.

115
00:10:18,436 --> 00:10:21,806
I'm sorry I tried to rule Earth.

116
00:10:21,981 --> 00:10:23,321
They'd be lucky to have you.

117
00:10:23,483 --> 00:10:26,323
I'm sorry about that thing
with the Tesseract.

118
00:10:26,653 --> 00:10:28,283
- I just couldn't help myself.
- I know.

119
00:10:28,446 --> 00:10:29,646
I'm a trickster.

120
00:10:29,823 --> 00:10:31,663
So mischievous.

121
00:10:31,950 --> 00:10:34,530
Sorry about that time I turned you
into a frog.

122
00:10:34,702 --> 00:10:36,122
It was a wonderful joke.

123
00:10:36,371 --> 00:10:38,412
'Twas indeed hilarious.

124
00:10:38,582 --> 00:10:40,792
You are the savior of Asgard.

125
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,790
- Tell my story.
- I will.

126
00:10:42,962 --> 00:10:44,212
Build a statue for me.

127
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:46,090
We will build a big statue for you.

128
00:10:46,257 --> 00:10:49,137
With my helmet on,
with the big bendy horns.

129
00:10:50,052 --> 00:10:52,262
I will tell Father
what you did here today.

130
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:54,140
I didn't do it for him.

131
00:10:55,015 --> 00:10:58,025
I didn't do it for him.

132
00:11:06,569 --> 00:11:08,859
No!

133
00:11:12,450 --> 00:11:15,280
And so, Loki died of his wounds,

134
00:11:15,453 --> 00:11:17,373
giving his life for ours.

135
00:11:17,538 --> 00:11:20,208
He fought back those disgusting elves,

136
00:11:20,374 --> 00:11:22,174
he brought peace to the realm.

137
00:11:22,334 --> 00:11:24,634
Loki, my boy...

138
00:11:25,296 --> 00:11:29,136
'Twas many moons ago I found you
on that frostbitten battlefield.

139
00:11:29,842 --> 00:11:32,382
On that day,
I did not yet see in you

140
00:11:32,553 --> 00:11:34,843
Asgard's savior. No.

141
00:11:35,014 --> 00:11:39,524
You were merely
a little blue baby icicle

142
00:11:40,311 --> 00:11:43,521
that melted this old fool's heart.

143
00:11:45,775 --> 00:11:48,485
Bravo! Bravo! Well done. Bravo.

144
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,280
Father.

145
00:11:55,326 --> 00:11:56,376
Shit.

146
00:11:56,827 --> 00:11:59,037
My son, Thor, has returned!

147
00:11:59,205 --> 00:12:00,705
Greetings, my boy.

148
00:12:02,416 --> 00:12:04,096
It's an interesting play.
What's it called?

149
00:12:04,251 --> 00:12:08,341
The Tragedy of Loki of Asgard.
The people wanted to commemorate him.

150
00:12:08,506 --> 00:12:09,806
Indeed they should.

151
00:12:09,965 --> 00:12:11,305
I like the statue.

152
00:12:11,467 --> 00:12:13,779
A lot better looking than he was
when he was alive, though.

153
00:12:13,803 --> 00:12:15,683
A little less weaselly, less greasy,
maybe.

154
00:12:16,931 --> 00:12:18,761
Do you know what this is?

155
00:12:19,683 --> 00:12:22,643
The skull of Surtur.
That's a formidable weapon!

156
00:12:22,812 --> 00:12:24,372
Do me a favor.
Lock this away in a vault

157
00:12:24,522 --> 00:12:27,732
so it doesn't turn into a giant monster
and destroy the whole planet.

158
00:12:28,984 --> 00:12:30,404
Thank you, dear.

159
00:12:30,986 --> 00:12:33,786
So it's back to Midgard for you, is it?

160
00:12:34,031 --> 00:12:35,071
Nope.

161
00:12:35,616 --> 00:12:38,286
I've been having this reoccurring dream
lately.

162
00:12:38,452 --> 00:12:41,242
Every night,
I see Asgard fall into ruins.

163
00:12:41,414 --> 00:12:42,544
That's just a silly dream,

164
00:12:42,706 --> 00:12:44,666
signs of an overactive imagination.

165
00:12:44,834 --> 00:12:45,834
Possibly.

166
00:12:45,919 --> 00:12:47,999
But then I decide to go out there
and investigate.

167
00:12:48,088 --> 00:12:52,138
And what do I find,
but the Nine Realms completely in chaos.

168
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,260
Enemies of Asgard assembling,
plotting our demise,

169
00:12:55,429 --> 00:12:58,349
all while you, Odin,
the protector of those Nine Realms,

170
00:12:58,515 --> 00:13:01,265
are sitting here in your bathrobe,
eating grapes.

171
00:13:01,435 --> 00:13:03,685
Yes, it is best
to respect our neighbors' freedom.

172
00:13:03,854 --> 00:13:06,854
Yes, of course,
the freedom to be massacred.

173
00:13:08,608 --> 00:13:10,688
Yes, besides I've been
rather busy myself.

174
00:13:10,861 --> 00:13:11,861
Watching theater.

175
00:13:12,028 --> 00:13:13,938
Board meetings,
and security council meetings...

176
00:13:14,114 --> 00:13:15,954
- You're really gonna make me do it?
- Do what?

177
00:13:20,162 --> 00:13:23,912
You know that nothing will stop Mjolnir
as it returns to my hand.

178
00:13:24,082 --> 00:13:25,542
Not even your face.

179
00:13:25,709 --> 00:13:27,959
You've gone quite mad.
You'll be executed for this.

180
00:13:28,128 --> 00:13:30,638
Then I'll see you on the other side,
brother.

181
00:13:32,174 --> 00:13:33,514
All right, I yield.

182
00:13:43,602 --> 00:13:44,602
Behold!

183
00:13:45,562 --> 00:13:46,772
Thor...

184
00:13:47,564 --> 00:13:48,944
- Odinson.
- No.

185
00:13:50,984 --> 00:13:52,944
You had one job. Just the one.

186
00:13:54,988 --> 00:13:56,108
Where's Odin?

187
00:13:56,281 --> 00:14:00,071
You just couldn't stay away, could you?
Everything was fine without you.

188
00:14:00,243 --> 00:14:02,913
Asgard was prospering.
You've ruined everything.

189
00:14:03,371 --> 00:14:05,211
- Ask them.
- Where's Father? Did you kill him?

190
00:14:05,248 --> 00:14:07,768
You had what you wanted.
You had the independence you asked for.

191
00:14:08,293 --> 00:14:10,713
Okay. I know exactly where he is.

192
00:14:22,849 --> 00:14:24,849
I swear I left him right here.

193
00:14:26,561 --> 00:14:29,332
Right here on the sidewalk, or right there
where the building is being demolished?

194
00:14:29,356 --> 00:14:30,486
Great planning.

195
00:14:30,565 --> 00:14:31,775
How was I supposed to know?

196
00:14:31,858 --> 00:14:33,503
Can't see into the future.
I'm not a witch.

197
00:14:33,527 --> 00:14:35,447
No? Then why do you dress like one?

198
00:14:35,946 --> 00:14:37,826
- Hey.
- I can't believe you're alive.

199
00:14:37,989 --> 00:14:40,989
I saw you die.
I mourned you, I cried for you.

200
00:14:41,326 --> 00:14:42,706
I'm honored.

201
00:14:42,869 --> 00:14:43,869
Ask him.

202
00:14:44,037 --> 00:14:45,757
Hi. Would you mind taking a picture
with us?

203
00:14:45,872 --> 00:14:46,872
Sure.

204
00:14:48,166 --> 00:14:49,666
Start figuring out where he is.

205
00:14:50,669 --> 00:14:51,669
Oh, my God.

206
00:14:51,753 --> 00:14:53,153
Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you.

207
00:14:53,964 --> 00:14:55,715
She didn't dump me, you know.

208
00:14:56,092 --> 00:14:58,012
I dumped her. It was a mutual dumping.

209
00:15:00,596 --> 00:15:01,976
What's this? What are you doing?

210
00:15:02,348 --> 00:15:03,358
This isn't me.

211
00:15:07,687 --> 00:15:08,687
Loki.

212
00:15:33,713 --> 00:15:35,753
Thor Odinson.

213
00:15:46,225 --> 00:15:47,855
God of Thunder.

214
00:15:48,978 --> 00:15:50,568
You can put down the umbrella.

215
00:16:08,164 --> 00:16:10,254
So, Earth has wizards now?

216
00:16:16,422 --> 00:16:18,382
The preferred term is
"Master of the Mystic Arts."

217
00:16:18,466 --> 00:16:19,466
You can leave that now.

218
00:16:20,635 --> 00:16:23,345
All right, wizard. Who are you?
Why should I care?

219
00:16:23,805 --> 00:16:27,855
My name is Doctor Stephen Strange,
and I have some questions for you.

220
00:16:28,101 --> 00:16:29,101
Take a seat.

221
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:35,270
Tea?

222
00:16:37,819 --> 00:16:39,029
I don't drink tea.

223
00:16:39,195 --> 00:16:40,405
What do you drink?

224
00:16:40,571 --> 00:16:41,781
Not tea.

225
00:16:44,992 --> 00:16:48,742
So, I keep a watch list of individuals
and beings from other realms

226
00:16:48,913 --> 00:16:50,313
that may be a threat to this world.

227
00:16:50,373 --> 00:16:54,083
Your adopted brother, Loki,
is one of those beings.

228
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:56,170
He's a worthy inclusion.

229
00:16:58,756 --> 00:17:00,506
Then why bring him here?

230
00:17:00,675 --> 00:17:02,305
We're looking for my father.

231
00:17:02,802 --> 00:17:06,013
So, if I were to tell you
where Odin was,

232
00:17:06,181 --> 00:17:08,511
all parties concerned
would promptly return to Asgard?

233
00:17:08,684 --> 00:17:09,684
Promptly.

234
00:17:09,852 --> 00:17:11,182
Great! Then I'll help you.

235
00:17:11,562 --> 00:17:13,562
If you knew where he was,
why didn't you call me?

236
00:17:14,231 --> 00:17:16,591
I have to tell you, he was adamant
that he not be disturbed.

237
00:17:16,733 --> 00:17:18,773
Your father said he had chosen
to remain in exile.

238
00:17:20,737 --> 00:17:23,037
And you don't have a phone.

239
00:17:23,490 --> 00:17:25,110
No, I don't have a phone,

240
00:17:25,284 --> 00:17:27,924
but you could have sent an electronic
letter. It's called an email.

241
00:17:28,036 --> 00:17:29,876
- Yeah, do you have a computer?
- No. What for?

242
00:17:31,248 --> 00:17:33,878
Anyway, my father is no longer in exile.

243
00:17:34,042 --> 00:17:36,792
So if you could tell me where he is,
I can take him home.

244
00:17:36,962 --> 00:17:38,832
Gladly. He's in Norway.

245
00:17:39,548 --> 00:17:45,098
I'm just seeing whether this incantation
requires any Asgardian modifications.

246
00:17:45,804 --> 00:17:46,844
Nope.

247
00:17:47,806 --> 00:17:48,936
We don't need that.

248
00:17:54,772 --> 00:17:56,182
Will you stop doing that?

249
00:17:58,317 --> 00:18:01,197
I need just one strand of your hair.

250
00:18:01,361 --> 00:18:04,151
Let me explain something.
My hair is not to be meddled with.

251
00:18:12,873 --> 00:18:14,163
We could have just walked.

252
00:18:16,919 --> 00:18:18,629
He's waiting for you.

253
00:18:18,796 --> 00:18:20,006
All right.

254
00:18:20,172 --> 00:18:21,632
Don't forget your umbrella.

255
00:18:21,799 --> 00:18:22,969
Yes.

256
00:18:30,766 --> 00:18:31,856
Sorry.

257
00:18:34,353 --> 00:18:36,103
There we go.

258
00:18:36,897 --> 00:18:38,567
I suppose I'll need my brother back.

259
00:18:39,525 --> 00:18:41,025
Yeah. Right.

260
00:18:46,281 --> 00:18:49,401
I have been falling for 30 minutes!

261
00:18:50,452 --> 00:18:51,702
You can handle him from here.

262
00:18:52,246 --> 00:18:54,786
Yes. Of course.
Thank you very much for your help.

263
00:18:54,957 --> 00:18:55,957
Good luck.

264
00:18:56,041 --> 00:18:58,121
Handle me? Who are you?

265
00:18:58,961 --> 00:18:59,961
Loki.

266
00:19:00,045 --> 00:19:01,439
You think you're some kind of sorcerer?

267
00:19:01,463 --> 00:19:03,149
Don't think for one minute,
you second-rate...

268
00:19:03,173 --> 00:19:04,173
Bye-bye.

269
00:19:29,659 --> 00:19:30,749
Father?

270
00:19:32,412 --> 00:19:34,992
Look at this place. It's beautiful.

271
00:19:40,295 --> 00:19:41,875
Father, it's us.

272
00:19:45,133 --> 00:19:46,753
My sons.

273
00:19:47,802 --> 00:19:49,052
I've been waiting for you.

274
00:19:49,429 --> 00:19:50,869
I know. We've come to take you home.

275
00:19:51,473 --> 00:19:52,803
Home, yes.

276
00:19:54,601 --> 00:19:56,771
Your mother, she calls me.

277
00:19:59,272 --> 00:20:00,272
Do you hear it?

278
00:20:02,317 --> 00:20:03,857
Loki, lift your magic.

279
00:20:06,529 --> 00:20:09,159
Took me quite a while
to break free from your spell.

280
00:20:09,324 --> 00:20:10,824
Frigga would have been proud.

281
00:20:10,992 --> 00:20:12,752
Come and sit with me.
I don't have much time.

282
00:20:20,210 --> 00:20:21,840
I know we failed you.

283
00:20:22,045 --> 00:20:23,425
But we can make this right.

284
00:20:24,089 --> 00:20:25,429
I failed you.

285
00:20:26,424 --> 00:20:28,674
It is upon us. Ragnarok.

286
00:20:29,302 --> 00:20:32,012
No, I've stopped Ragnarok.
I put an end to Surtur.

287
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:33,730
No.

288
00:20:34,265 --> 00:20:36,345
It has already begun. She's coming.

289
00:20:37,644 --> 00:20:40,814
My life was all that held her back.
But my time has come.

290
00:20:43,817 --> 00:20:45,317
I cannot keep her away any longer.

291
00:20:45,902 --> 00:20:47,442
Father, who are you talking about?

292
00:20:48,154 --> 00:20:51,074
Goddess of Death. Hela.

293
00:20:52,158 --> 00:20:53,708
My firstborn.

294
00:20:54,828 --> 00:20:55,828
Your sister.

295
00:20:58,915 --> 00:21:00,665
Your what?

296
00:21:03,128 --> 00:21:05,968
Her violent appetites
grew beyond my control.

297
00:21:07,132 --> 00:21:11,422
I couldn't stop her, so I imprisoned her.
Locked her away.

298
00:21:12,595 --> 00:21:15,725
She draws her strength from Asgard,

299
00:21:16,933 --> 00:21:20,563
and once she gets there,
her powers will be limitless.

300
00:21:21,146 --> 00:21:23,500
Whatever she is, we can stop her together.
We can face her together.

301
00:21:23,524 --> 00:21:24,524
No, we won't.

302
00:21:25,818 --> 00:21:27,818
I'm on a different path now.

303
00:21:27,987 --> 00:21:29,447
This you must face alone.

304
00:21:31,949 --> 00:21:33,539
I love you, my sons.

305
00:21:36,245 --> 00:21:37,745
Look at that.

306
00:21:41,667 --> 00:21:43,337
Remember this place.

307
00:21:44,879 --> 00:21:46,379
Home.

308
00:22:26,212 --> 00:22:27,302
Brother.

309
00:22:35,096 --> 00:22:37,806
This was your doing.

310
00:23:20,266 --> 00:23:21,596
So he's gone.

311
00:23:25,271 --> 00:23:27,611
That's a shame.
I would've liked to have seen that.

312
00:23:28,065 --> 00:23:29,605
You must be Hela.

313
00:23:31,277 --> 00:23:32,568
I'm Thor, son of Odin.

314
00:23:32,904 --> 00:23:36,234
Really? You don't look like him.

315
00:23:36,700 --> 00:23:38,450
Perhaps we can come to an arrangement.

316
00:23:38,618 --> 00:23:40,498
You sound like him.

317
00:23:42,497 --> 00:23:43,577
Kneel.

318
00:23:43,749 --> 00:23:45,089
Beg your pardon?

319
00:23:49,421 --> 00:23:50,971
Kneel.

320
00:23:54,176 --> 00:23:55,926
Before your queen.

321
00:23:57,220 --> 00:23:58,600
I don't think so.

322
00:24:09,316 --> 00:24:11,436
It's not possible.

323
00:24:12,569 --> 00:24:16,239
Darling, you have no idea
what's possible.

324
00:24:36,176 --> 00:24:37,346
Bring us back!

325
00:24:37,511 --> 00:24:38,511
No!

326
00:24:47,604 --> 00:24:48,684
Loki!

327
00:25:35,777 --> 00:25:37,417
Who are you?
What have you done with Thor?

328
00:25:42,535 --> 00:25:43,695
I'm Hela.

329
00:25:45,955 --> 00:25:47,615
I'm just a janitor.

330
00:25:49,041 --> 00:25:52,211
You look like a smart boy
with good survival instincts.

331
00:25:55,173 --> 00:25:56,973
How would you like a job?

332
00:28:08,348 --> 00:28:09,928
Are you a fighter?

333
00:28:10,726 --> 00:28:12,096
Or are you food?

334
00:28:12,644 --> 00:28:14,194
I'm just passing through.

335
00:28:14,855 --> 00:28:16,275
It is food.

336
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,570
On your knees.

337
00:29:00,526 --> 00:29:01,776
He's mine.

338
00:29:10,994 --> 00:29:12,124
Wait!

339
00:29:20,921 --> 00:29:22,131
Wait!

340
00:29:24,383 --> 00:29:25,473
He's mine.

341
00:29:25,634 --> 00:29:28,854
So if you want him, you go through me.

342
00:29:29,012 --> 00:29:30,432
But we've already got him.

343
00:29:32,224 --> 00:29:35,064
All right, then.
I guess I go through you.

344
00:29:35,602 --> 00:29:37,062
More food.

345
00:30:12,766 --> 00:30:13,776
Thank you.

346
00:30:49,010 --> 00:30:52,600
Scrapper 142. I need clearance
and an audience with the boss.

347
00:30:53,056 --> 00:30:54,856
I've got something special.

348
00:30:55,016 --> 00:30:57,346
Hey! Where are you taking me?

349
00:30:58,645 --> 00:30:59,985
Answer me!

350
00:31:00,271 --> 00:31:01,481
Hey!

351
00:31:01,648 --> 00:31:04,268
I am Thor, son of Odin.
I need to get back to Asgard.

352
00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:07,280
Many apologies, your majesty.

353
00:31:36,182 --> 00:31:39,852
It's come to my attention
that you don't know who I am.

354
00:31:46,818 --> 00:31:50,358
I am Hela, Odin's firstborn,

355
00:31:50,530 --> 00:31:52,910
the commander
of the Legions of Asgard,

356
00:31:53,074 --> 00:31:56,454
the rightful heir to the throne,
and the Goddess of Death.

357
00:32:00,999 --> 00:32:03,629
My father is dead.

358
00:32:03,793 --> 00:32:05,673
As are the princes.
You're welcome.

359
00:32:06,296 --> 00:32:09,767
We were once the seat
of absolute power in the Cosmos.

360
00:32:09,925 --> 00:32:12,095
Our supremacy was unchallenged.

361
00:32:12,261 --> 00:32:15,351
Yet Odin stopped at Nine Realms.

362
00:32:15,514 --> 00:32:18,934
Our destiny is to rule over all others.

363
00:32:19,769 --> 00:32:22,889
And I am here to restore that power.

364
00:32:24,273 --> 00:32:25,903
Kneel before me

365
00:32:26,066 --> 00:32:30,116
and rise into the ranks
of my great conquest.

366
00:32:31,489 --> 00:32:33,239
Whoever you are,

367
00:32:33,407 --> 00:32:36,407
whatever you've done, surrender now!

368
00:32:36,577 --> 00:32:38,797
Or we will show you no mercy.

369
00:32:38,954 --> 00:32:43,164
Whoever I am?
Did you listen to a word I said?

370
00:32:43,334 --> 00:32:45,384
This is your last warning!

371
00:32:47,630 --> 00:32:49,840
I thought you'd be happy to see me.

372
00:32:55,429 --> 00:32:56,719
Fine.

373
00:33:10,027 --> 00:33:11,437
Charge!

374
00:34:05,833 --> 00:34:07,833
I've missed this.

375
00:34:08,169 --> 00:34:09,919
Still, it's a shame.

376
00:34:10,296 --> 00:34:12,506
Good soldiers dying for nothing,

377
00:34:12,590 --> 00:34:14,880
all because
they couldn't see the future.

378
00:34:15,176 --> 00:34:16,516
Sad.

379
00:34:18,095 --> 00:34:19,766
Look, still alive.

380
00:34:27,314 --> 00:34:29,024
Change of heart?

381
00:34:29,191 --> 00:34:31,651
Go back to whatever cave
you crept out of.

382
00:34:32,861 --> 00:34:34,321
You evil demoness!

383
00:34:38,366 --> 00:34:40,416
Let's go see my palace.

384
00:35:11,274 --> 00:35:13,614
Fear not, for you are found.

385
00:35:15,695 --> 00:35:17,655
You are home,
and there is no going back.

386
00:35:20,534 --> 00:35:23,034
No one leaves this place.

387
00:35:23,203 --> 00:35:24,873
But what is this place?

388
00:35:25,038 --> 00:35:28,248
The answer is Sakaar.

389
00:35:30,127 --> 00:35:31,587
Surrounded by cosmic gateways,

390
00:35:32,462 --> 00:35:35,302
Sakaar lives on the edge
of the known and unknown.

391
00:35:35,465 --> 00:35:39,015
It is the collection point
for all lost and unloved things.

392
00:35:39,177 --> 00:35:40,887
Like you.

393
00:35:41,054 --> 00:35:43,804
But here on Sakaar, you are significant.

394
00:35:43,974 --> 00:35:45,474
You are valuable.

395
00:35:45,642 --> 00:35:47,022
Here you are loved.

396
00:35:47,185 --> 00:35:48,185
What the hell?

397
00:35:48,353 --> 00:35:51,483
And no one loves you more
than the Grandmaster.

398
00:35:51,648 --> 00:35:55,818
He is the original,
the first lost and the first found.

399
00:35:55,986 --> 00:35:57,156
The creator of Sakaar,

400
00:35:57,320 --> 00:36:00,570
and father of the Contest of Champions.

401
00:36:00,740 --> 00:36:05,030
Where once you were nothing,
now you are something.

402
00:36:05,203 --> 00:36:08,373
You are the property of the Grandmaster.

403
00:36:08,540 --> 00:36:10,000
Congratulations!

404
00:36:10,167 --> 00:36:13,677
You will meet the Grandmaster
in five seconds.

405
00:36:14,045 --> 00:36:15,425
Prepare yourself.

406
00:36:17,174 --> 00:36:18,424
Prepare yourself.

407
00:36:20,218 --> 00:36:23,508
You are now meeting the Grandmaster.

408
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:38,537
He's wonderful.
It is a he?

409
00:36:38,738 --> 00:36:39,998
It is a he.

410
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:41,156
Yeah.

411
00:36:41,240 --> 00:36:43,240
I love when you come to visit, 142.

412
00:36:43,326 --> 00:36:44,956
You bring me the best stuff.

413
00:36:45,119 --> 00:36:48,659
Whenever we get to talking, Topaz,
about Scrapper 142,

414
00:36:48,831 --> 00:36:52,371
what do I always say? "She is the..."
And it starts with a "B."

415
00:36:52,543 --> 00:36:53,583
Trash.

416
00:36:54,587 --> 00:36:56,467
No, not trash.

417
00:36:57,256 --> 00:37:00,306
Were you waiting just to call her that?
It doesn't start with a "B."

418
00:37:00,468 --> 00:37:01,598
Booze hag.

419
00:37:04,263 --> 00:37:06,603
I'm so sorry. No, "best."
I was thinking about "best."

420
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:08,118
'Cause I always say you're the best.

421
00:37:08,142 --> 00:37:10,062
She brought me my beloved champion,
you know.

422
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:12,028
You say that every time she's here.

423
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,668
What have you brought today? Tell me.

424
00:37:13,815 --> 00:37:14,815
A contender.

425
00:37:14,982 --> 00:37:16,062
A what?

426
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:18,378
I need to go closer.
I want to get a closer look at this.

427
00:37:18,402 --> 00:37:20,362
Can you take us closer? Thank you.

428
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:33,917
Pay this lady.

429
00:37:34,085 --> 00:37:35,835
Just wait a damn minute.

430
00:37:36,003 --> 00:37:38,423
I'm not for sale.

431
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:46,307
Man, he's a fighter.

432
00:37:46,472 --> 00:37:47,802
I take 10 million.

433
00:37:47,974 --> 00:37:49,014
Tell her she's dreaming.

434
00:37:49,183 --> 00:37:51,143
For heaven's sakes, transfer the units.

435
00:37:58,151 --> 00:37:59,731
You'll pay for this.

436
00:37:59,902 --> 00:38:01,272
No, I got paid for this.

437
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:04,654
Here's what I wanna know.

438
00:38:06,325 --> 00:38:07,325
Who are you?

439
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:11,580
I am the God of Thunder.

440
00:38:14,792 --> 00:38:18,252
I didn't hear any thunder, but out of your
fingers, was that sparkles?

441
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:20,798
We've located your cousin.

442
00:38:21,716 --> 00:38:22,806
Good!

443
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:25,137
Yeah, come on.
I think you're gonna like this.

444
00:38:25,303 --> 00:38:26,303
There he is.

445
00:38:26,387 --> 00:38:27,637
Hey, cuz.

446
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:30,519
We almost couldn't find you.
What, you been hiding?

447
00:38:30,683 --> 00:38:31,683
Hi.

448
00:38:33,394 --> 00:38:34,604
So...

449
00:38:34,771 --> 00:38:35,851
Please.

450
00:38:37,064 --> 00:38:38,065
I'm sorry.

451
00:38:38,233 --> 00:38:39,403
Yeah.

452
00:38:39,568 --> 00:38:40,818
Carlo...

453
00:38:41,945 --> 00:38:43,155
I pardon you.

454
00:38:43,322 --> 00:38:44,692
Thank you.

455
00:38:44,865 --> 00:38:45,865
Thank you.

456
00:38:46,200 --> 00:38:49,080
You're officially pardoned.
From life.

457
00:38:54,792 --> 00:38:56,042
Help me.

458
00:38:56,877 --> 00:38:59,507
Oh, my God!

459
00:38:59,671 --> 00:39:01,671
I'm stepping in it.
I'm stepping in it. Look!

460
00:39:04,051 --> 00:39:05,631
The smell.

461
00:39:06,053 --> 00:39:07,263
What does it smell like?

462
00:39:07,429 --> 00:39:08,639
Burnt toast.

463
00:39:09,681 --> 00:39:11,471
What happened to my manners?

464
00:39:11,767 --> 00:39:13,317
I haven't properly introduced myself.

465
00:39:13,477 --> 00:39:15,397
Come on. Follow me.

466
00:39:15,813 --> 00:39:17,813
My name is Grandmaster.

467
00:39:17,981 --> 00:39:21,401
I preside over a little harlequinade
called the Contest of Champions.

468
00:39:21,568 --> 00:39:24,278
People come from far and wide
to unwillingly participate in it.

469
00:39:24,446 --> 00:39:27,156
And you, my friend,
might just be part of the new cast.

470
00:39:27,324 --> 00:39:28,324
What do you say to that?

471
00:39:28,408 --> 00:39:30,637
We're not friends and I don't give a shit
about your games.

472
00:39:30,661 --> 00:39:31,991
I'm going back to Asgard.

473
00:39:32,204 --> 00:39:33,664
Ass-gard.

474
00:39:35,082 --> 00:39:37,252
One, two, three, four.

475
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:40,870
There was a wormhole
in space and time beneath me.

476
00:39:41,046 --> 00:39:43,966
At that moment, I let go.

477
00:39:44,425 --> 00:39:45,555
Loki?

478
00:39:46,844 --> 00:39:48,554
Loki! Loki!

479
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:50,590
Over here. Over here.

480
00:39:52,182 --> 00:39:53,552
- Excuse me one second.
- Loki!

481
00:39:55,436 --> 00:39:56,516
- What?
- You're alive?

482
00:39:56,687 --> 00:39:58,623
- Yes, of course I'm alive.
- What are you doing here?

483
00:39:58,647 --> 00:40:00,792
What do you mean, what am I doing?
I'm stuck in this stupid chair.

484
00:40:00,816 --> 00:40:02,502
- Where's your chair?
- I didn't get a chair.

485
00:40:02,526 --> 00:40:04,254
- Get me out of this one. Get me out.
- I can't.

486
00:40:04,278 --> 00:40:05,488
- I can't.
- What?

487
00:40:05,654 --> 00:40:07,340
I've made friends with this man.
He's called the Grandmaster.

488
00:40:07,364 --> 00:40:08,842
- He's crazy!
- I've gained his favor.

489
00:40:08,866 --> 00:40:10,506
The Bifrost brought me out here
weeks ago.

490
00:40:10,617 --> 00:40:11,747
- Weeks ago?
- Yes.

491
00:40:11,910 --> 00:40:12,910
I just got here.

492
00:40:13,078 --> 00:40:14,278
What are you whispering about?

493
00:40:15,372 --> 00:40:17,132
Time works real different
around these parts.

494
00:40:17,291 --> 00:40:20,331
On any other world, I'd be, like,
millions of years old.

495
00:40:20,502 --> 00:40:22,122
But here on Sakaar...

496
00:40:27,551 --> 00:40:30,221
In any case, you know this...

497
00:40:30,387 --> 00:40:31,747
You call yourself Lord of Thunder?

498
00:40:31,805 --> 00:40:34,145
God of Thunder.
Tell him.

499
00:40:34,308 --> 00:40:35,978
I've never met this man in my life.

500
00:40:36,143 --> 00:40:37,763
- He's my brother.
- Adopted.

501
00:40:37,936 --> 00:40:39,066
Is he any kind of a fighter?

502
00:40:39,563 --> 00:40:41,499
You take this thing out of my neck
and I'll show you.

503
00:40:41,523 --> 00:40:43,233
Now, listen to that.
He's threatening me.

504
00:40:43,400 --> 00:40:45,360
Hey, Sparkles, here's the deal.

505
00:40:45,527 --> 00:40:47,778
If you wanna get back to Ass-place,
Assberg...

506
00:40:47,864 --> 00:40:48,864
Asgard.

507
00:40:48,948 --> 00:40:52,038
Any contender who defeats my champion,

508
00:40:52,118 --> 00:40:53,958
their freedom they shall win.

509
00:40:54,120 --> 00:40:57,340
Fine. Then point me in the direction
of whoever's ass I have to kick!

510
00:40:57,499 --> 00:41:00,049
That's what I call, contender.

511
00:41:00,210 --> 00:41:02,630
Direction would be this way, Lord.

512
00:41:03,338 --> 00:41:04,338
Loki!

513
00:41:10,512 --> 00:41:12,172
Hey. Take it easy, man.

514
00:41:13,848 --> 00:41:14,848
Over here.

515
00:41:15,016 --> 00:41:16,606
The pile of rocks waving at you. Here.

516
00:41:16,768 --> 00:41:19,318
Yeah, I'm actually a thing. I'm a being.

517
00:41:19,479 --> 00:41:20,539
Allow me to introduce myself.

518
00:41:20,563 --> 00:41:22,643
My name is Korg.
I'm kind of like the leader in here.

519
00:41:22,732 --> 00:41:26,152
I'm made of rocks, as you can see.
But don't let that intimidate you.

520
00:41:26,319 --> 00:41:29,239
You don't need to be afraid
unless you're made of scissors.

521
00:41:29,405 --> 00:41:31,695
Just a little rock-paper-scissor joke
for you.

522
00:41:31,866 --> 00:41:34,616
This is my very good friend over here,
Miek.

523
00:41:34,786 --> 00:41:37,536
He's an insect and has knives for hands.

524
00:41:38,164 --> 00:41:39,624
You're a Kronan, aren't you?

525
00:41:39,791 --> 00:41:42,381
- That I am.
- How'd you end up in here?

526
00:41:42,544 --> 00:41:45,504
Well, I tried to start a revolution,
but didn't print enough pamphlets.

527
00:41:45,672 --> 00:41:49,842
So hardly anyone turned up, except for
my mum and her boyfriend, who I hate.

528
00:41:50,009 --> 00:41:53,849
As punishment, I was forced
to be in here and become a gladiator.

529
00:41:54,013 --> 00:41:55,613
Bit of a promotional disaster, that one.

530
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:58,360
But I'm actually organizing
another revolution.

531
00:41:58,518 --> 00:42:00,579
I don't know if you'd be interested
in something like that.

532
00:42:00,603 --> 00:42:02,523
Do you reckon you'd be interested?

533
00:42:04,691 --> 00:42:05,781
How did you...

534
00:42:05,942 --> 00:42:08,652
Yeah, no. This whole thing is a circle.

535
00:42:08,820 --> 00:42:11,990
But not a real circle,
more like a freaky circle.

536
00:42:12,157 --> 00:42:14,827
- This doesn't make any sense.
- No, nothing makes sense here, man.

537
00:42:14,993 --> 00:42:17,993
The only thing that does make sense
is that nothing makes sense.

538
00:42:18,163 --> 00:42:20,493
Has anyone here fought
the Grandmaster's champion?

539
00:42:20,665 --> 00:42:21,745
Doug has.

540
00:42:21,916 --> 00:42:22,916
Doug!

541
00:42:23,084 --> 00:42:24,254
Our luck, Doug's dead.

542
00:42:24,419 --> 00:42:25,419
That's right.

543
00:42:25,503 --> 00:42:27,923
Everyone who fights
the Grandmaster's champion perishes.

544
00:42:28,006 --> 00:42:29,676
What about you? You're made of rocks.

545
00:42:29,841 --> 00:42:32,511
Perishable rock.
There you go. Another one gone.

546
00:42:32,677 --> 00:42:36,517
Yeah, no, I just do the smaller fights,
warm up the crowd and whatnot.

547
00:42:36,681 --> 00:42:38,431
Wait. You're not gonna face him,
are you?

548
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:40,060
Yes, I am.

549
00:42:40,226 --> 00:42:43,476
Gonna fight him, win,
and get the hell out of this place.

550
00:42:44,105 --> 00:42:46,025
That's exactly what Doug used to say.

551
00:42:46,191 --> 00:42:48,031
See you later, new Doug.

552
00:42:57,828 --> 00:42:59,578
Does no one remember me?

553
00:43:00,247 --> 00:43:02,707
Has no one been taught our history?

554
00:43:08,297 --> 00:43:09,757
Look at these lies.

555
00:43:10,466 --> 00:43:11,926
Goblets and garden parties?

556
00:43:14,136 --> 00:43:15,806
Peace treaties?

557
00:43:16,597 --> 00:43:17,847
Odin...

558
00:43:18,015 --> 00:43:19,635
Proud to have it,

559
00:43:19,809 --> 00:43:21,189
ashamed of how he got it.

560
00:43:40,287 --> 00:43:42,537
We were unstoppable.

561
00:43:42,706 --> 00:43:47,296
I was his weapon in the conquest
that built Asgard's empire.

562
00:43:50,047 --> 00:43:53,427
One by one, the realms became ours.

563
00:43:53,592 --> 00:43:57,802
But then,
simply because my ambition outgrew his,

564
00:43:57,972 --> 00:44:02,652
he banished me, caged me,
locked me away like an animal.

565
00:44:02,893 --> 00:44:05,683
Before that,
Asgard's warriors were honored,

566
00:44:05,855 --> 00:44:09,485
their bodies buried as heroes
beneath this very palace.

567
00:44:20,619 --> 00:44:22,419
- Odin's treasures.
- Fake.

568
00:44:24,582 --> 00:44:27,132
Most of the stuff in here is fake.

569
00:44:27,710 --> 00:44:28,920
Or weak.

570
00:44:31,005 --> 00:44:33,005
Smaller than I thought it would be.

571
00:44:34,091 --> 00:44:35,971
That's not bad.

572
00:44:36,135 --> 00:44:37,425
But this...

573
00:44:38,012 --> 00:44:40,142
The Eternal Flame.

574
00:45:08,293 --> 00:45:10,543
Want to see what true power
really looks like?

575
00:45:39,491 --> 00:45:42,161
Fenris, my darling,
what have they done to you?

576
00:45:44,621 --> 00:45:48,711
With the Eternal Flame, you are reborn.

577
00:46:04,307 --> 00:46:06,227
I've missed you.

578
00:46:07,060 --> 00:46:08,980
I've missed you all.

579
00:46:11,690 --> 00:46:12,730
Odin,

580
00:46:12,983 --> 00:46:16,283
I bid you take your place
in the halls of Valhalla,

581
00:46:16,445 --> 00:46:18,815
where the brave shall live forever.

582
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:22,660
Nor shall we mourn but rejoice,

583
00:46:22,826 --> 00:46:25,536
for those that have died
the glorious death.

584
00:46:33,587 --> 00:46:35,007
Hurts, doesn't it?

585
00:46:35,172 --> 00:46:36,172
Being lied to.

586
00:46:37,215 --> 00:46:40,635
Being told you're one thing
and then learning it's all a fiction.

587
00:46:45,474 --> 00:46:47,594
You didn't think
I'd really come and see you, did you?

588
00:46:47,642 --> 00:46:49,402
This place is disgusting.

589
00:46:52,272 --> 00:46:54,152
Does this mean you don't want my help?

590
00:46:54,316 --> 00:46:56,461
Look, I couldn't jeopardize my position
with the Grandmaster.

591
00:46:56,485 --> 00:46:59,445
It took me time to win his trust.
He's a lunatic, but he can be amenable.

592
00:46:59,613 --> 00:47:02,873
What I'm telling you is, you could
join me at the Grandmaster's side.

593
00:47:03,033 --> 00:47:07,663
Perhaps, in time, an accident befalls
the Grandmaster, and then...

594
00:47:13,835 --> 00:47:16,206
You're not seriously thinking
of going back, are you?

595
00:47:18,508 --> 00:47:22,638
Our sister destroyed your hammer
like a piece of glass.

596
00:47:23,554 --> 00:47:25,491
She's stronger than both of us.
She's stronger than you.

597
00:47:25,515 --> 00:47:26,925
You don't stand a chance.

598
00:47:27,100 --> 00:47:29,270
Do you understand
what I'm saying here?

599
00:47:33,689 --> 00:47:34,769
Fine.

600
00:47:37,401 --> 00:47:39,991
I guess I'll just have to go it alone.

601
00:47:40,905 --> 00:47:41,905
Like I've always done.

602
00:47:44,909 --> 00:47:46,199
Would you say something?

603
00:47:48,871 --> 00:47:50,421
Say something!

604
00:47:51,541 --> 00:47:53,751
What would you like me to say?

605
00:47:54,127 --> 00:47:56,337
You faked your own death,

606
00:47:56,504 --> 00:47:59,014
you stole the throne,
stripped Odin of his power,

607
00:47:59,173 --> 00:48:02,473
stranded him on Earth to die,
releasing the Goddess of Death.

608
00:48:02,969 --> 00:48:06,349
Have I said enough or would you like me
to go back further than the past two days?

609
00:48:07,974 --> 00:48:11,564
You know, I haven't seen this
beloved champion he talks of,

610
00:48:11,727 --> 00:48:13,727
but I've heard
he is astonishingly savage.

611
00:48:14,439 --> 00:48:17,109
I've placed a large wager against you
tomorrow.

612
00:48:18,359 --> 00:48:19,489
Don't let me down.

613
00:48:23,448 --> 00:48:24,948
Piss off, ghost!

614
00:48:27,410 --> 00:48:29,000
He's freaking gone.

615
00:48:37,295 --> 00:48:38,295
Yuck!

616
00:48:38,463 --> 00:48:40,543
There's still someone's hair and blood
all over this.

617
00:48:40,673 --> 00:48:43,393
Guys, can you clean up the weapons
once you finish your fight?

618
00:48:43,551 --> 00:48:44,551
Disgusting slobs.

619
00:48:46,179 --> 00:48:47,349
Thor,

620
00:48:47,513 --> 00:48:49,523
wanna use a big wooden fork?

621
00:48:50,016 --> 00:48:51,016
No.

622
00:48:51,100 --> 00:48:52,270
Yeah, not really useful.

623
00:48:52,393 --> 00:48:55,903
Unless you're fighting off three vampires
that were huddled together.

624
00:48:56,564 --> 00:48:58,234
I really wish I had my hammer.

625
00:48:58,649 --> 00:48:59,649
Hammer?

626
00:48:59,734 --> 00:49:00,744
Quite unique.

627
00:49:00,818 --> 00:49:03,528
It was made from this special metal
from the heart of a dying star.

628
00:49:04,071 --> 00:49:06,871
And when I spun it really, really fast,
it gave me the ability to fly.

629
00:49:07,033 --> 00:49:08,163
You rode a hammer?

630
00:49:08,326 --> 00:49:09,866
No, I didn't ride the hammer.

631
00:49:10,036 --> 00:49:11,356
The hammer rode you on your back?

632
00:49:11,496 --> 00:49:14,866
No. I used to spin it really fast,
and it would pull me off the...

633
00:49:15,041 --> 00:49:17,041
Oh, my God. A hammer pulled you off?

634
00:49:17,210 --> 00:49:20,920
The ground. It would pull me off the
ground, up into the air, and I would fly.

635
00:49:21,089 --> 00:49:24,090
Every time I threw it,
it would always come back to me.

636
00:49:24,259 --> 00:49:27,072
Sounds like you had a pretty special
and intimate relationship with this hammer

637
00:49:27,096 --> 00:49:30,216
and that losing it was almost comparable
to losing a loved one.

638
00:49:31,141 --> 00:49:33,351
That's a nice way of putting it.

639
00:49:34,978 --> 00:49:36,348
I said they're mine.

640
00:49:37,689 --> 00:49:39,689
See her,
that's the one that put me in here.

641
00:49:39,858 --> 00:49:42,028
Yeah. Scrapper 142.

642
00:49:42,194 --> 00:49:44,244
Gotta watch out
for those Asgardians, man.

643
00:49:44,404 --> 00:49:46,074
They are hard to perish.

644
00:49:46,240 --> 00:49:47,700
Asgardian?

645
00:49:49,243 --> 00:49:50,243
Hey.

646
00:49:50,452 --> 00:49:51,452
Hey.

647
00:49:52,121 --> 00:49:53,121
Hey.

648
00:49:53,580 --> 00:49:56,000
Do not zap me with that thing.
I just wanna talk.

649
00:49:57,751 --> 00:49:59,171
Asgard is in danger.

650
00:50:03,632 --> 00:50:05,222
My God, you're a Valkyrie.

651
00:50:06,677 --> 00:50:08,530
I used to wanna be a Valkyrie
when I was younger,

652
00:50:08,554 --> 00:50:10,894
until I found out that
you were all women.

653
00:50:11,056 --> 00:50:13,337
There's nothing wrong with women,
of course. I love women.

654
00:50:13,392 --> 00:50:14,942
Sometimes a little too much.

655
00:50:15,102 --> 00:50:18,102
Not in a creepy way,
just more of a respectful appreciation.

656
00:50:18,272 --> 00:50:22,732
I think it's great that there is
an elite force of women warriors.

657
00:50:22,901 --> 00:50:24,401
It's about time.

658
00:50:25,988 --> 00:50:26,988
Are you done?

659
00:50:27,072 --> 00:50:28,133
Lord of Thunder, you're up.

660
00:50:28,157 --> 00:50:29,259
Please, help me. I need your help.

661
00:50:29,283 --> 00:50:30,283
Bye.

662
00:50:30,451 --> 00:50:32,621
Fine, then you must be a traitor
or a coward.

663
00:50:32,786 --> 00:50:35,116
Because the Valkyrie is sworn to protect
the throne.

664
00:50:35,831 --> 00:50:39,131
Listen closely, your majesty.
This is Sakaar, not Asgard.

665
00:50:39,293 --> 00:50:41,133
And I'm a Scrapper, not a Valkyrie.

666
00:50:44,423 --> 00:50:46,343
Bring him in for processing.

667
00:50:46,508 --> 00:50:50,388
And no one escapes this place.
So you're gonna die anyway.

668
00:51:02,274 --> 00:51:03,864
Now, don't you move.

669
00:51:04,026 --> 00:51:06,646
My hands ain't as steady
as they used to be.

670
00:51:06,820 --> 00:51:09,820
By Odin's beard,
you shall not cut my hair,

671
00:51:09,990 --> 00:51:12,410
lest you feel the wrath
of the mighty Thor.

672
00:51:16,830 --> 00:51:19,330
Please.
Please, kind sir, do not cut my hair.

673
00:51:20,584 --> 00:51:21,964
Please! No!

674
00:51:22,127 --> 00:51:23,247
No!

675
00:51:35,475 --> 00:51:39,815
Look at all of you.
What a show! What a night!

676
00:51:39,979 --> 00:51:40,979
Who's having fun?

677
00:51:42,148 --> 00:51:44,108
Please, I'm your host.

678
00:51:44,275 --> 00:51:47,495
Big round of applause
for all of our undercard competitors,

679
00:51:47,654 --> 00:51:50,454
who today died so gruesomely.

680
00:51:50,615 --> 00:51:51,825
Good sports.

681
00:51:51,991 --> 00:51:53,661
What a show! What a night!

682
00:51:54,619 --> 00:51:58,039
This is what you've come for,
and so have I.

683
00:52:03,711 --> 00:52:06,711
And now, without further ado,

684
00:52:06,881 --> 00:52:09,381
it's main event time.

685
00:52:11,094 --> 00:52:14,434
Making his first appearance,
though he looks quite promising,

686
00:52:14,597 --> 00:52:16,427
got a couple of tricks up his sleeve.

687
00:52:17,016 --> 00:52:19,636
I'll say no more, see what you think.

688
00:52:19,811 --> 00:52:21,211
Ladies and gentlemen, I give you...

689
00:52:22,313 --> 00:52:24,523
Lord of Thunder.

690
00:52:47,839 --> 00:52:50,549
Watch out for his fingers.
They make sparks.

691
00:52:50,717 --> 00:52:51,837
Okay, this is it.

692
00:52:52,010 --> 00:52:54,840
Let's get ready to welcome this guy.
Here he comes.

693
00:53:03,772 --> 00:53:05,232
He is a creature.

694
00:53:05,398 --> 00:53:07,108
What can we say about him?

695
00:53:07,275 --> 00:53:09,155
Well, he's unique.
There's none like him.

696
00:53:09,319 --> 00:53:12,069
I feel a special connection with him.

697
00:53:13,615 --> 00:53:14,865
He's undefeated.

698
00:53:16,451 --> 00:53:17,871
He's the reigning.

699
00:53:20,246 --> 00:53:22,406
He's the defending.

700
00:53:22,832 --> 00:53:23,962
Ladies and gentlemen...

701
00:53:24,125 --> 00:53:25,175
I give you...

702
00:53:30,131 --> 00:53:33,881
Your Incredible...

703
00:53:37,639 --> 00:53:39,349
Hulk!

704
00:53:40,100 --> 00:53:41,430
Yes!

705
00:53:45,356 --> 00:53:47,316
I have to get off this planet.

706
00:53:47,942 --> 00:53:49,822
Hey, hey, hey. Where you going?

707
00:53:57,910 --> 00:53:59,200
Hey!

708
00:53:59,912 --> 00:54:01,162
We know each other.

709
00:54:01,622 --> 00:54:03,622
He's a friend from work.

710
00:54:12,800 --> 00:54:14,220
Where have you been?

711
00:54:14,385 --> 00:54:16,515
Everybody thought you were dead.

712
00:54:16,679 --> 00:54:18,679
But so much has happened
since I last saw you.

713
00:54:19,473 --> 00:54:20,893
I lost my hammer.

714
00:54:21,058 --> 00:54:24,098
Like, yesterday,
so that's still pretty fresh.

715
00:54:24,270 --> 00:54:26,600
Loki. Loki's alive. Can you believe it?

716
00:54:26,772 --> 00:54:27,852
He's up there.

717
00:54:28,023 --> 00:54:30,073
Loki! Look who it is!

718
00:54:32,194 --> 00:54:34,364
Banner,
I never thought I would say this,

719
00:54:34,530 --> 00:54:36,780
but I'm happy to see you.

720
00:54:36,949 --> 00:54:39,449
Hulk! Hulk! Hulk!

721
00:54:45,416 --> 00:54:46,416
Banner.

722
00:54:47,376 --> 00:54:48,756
Hey, Banner!

723
00:54:49,170 --> 00:54:51,290
No Banner. Only Hulk.

724
00:54:51,672 --> 00:54:53,172
What are you doing?

725
00:54:53,340 --> 00:54:54,840
It's me. It's Thor!

726
00:55:15,029 --> 00:55:16,319
Banner, we're friends.

727
00:55:16,489 --> 00:55:18,049
This is crazy.
I don't want to hurt you!

728
00:55:25,372 --> 00:55:27,412
Here we go.

729
00:55:46,268 --> 00:55:47,388
What?

730
00:55:57,864 --> 00:55:59,364
Hey, big guy.

731
00:56:01,201 --> 00:56:03,241
The sun's getting real low.

732
00:56:13,964 --> 00:56:16,844
That's it.
The sun's going down.

733
00:56:19,594 --> 00:56:21,554
I won't hurt you anymore.

734
00:56:21,721 --> 00:56:23,261
No one will.

735
00:56:35,068 --> 00:56:36,068
Yes!

736
00:56:36,153 --> 00:56:37,283
That's how it feels!

737
00:56:38,697 --> 00:56:40,537
I'm just a huge fan of the sport.

738
00:56:48,248 --> 00:56:50,668
All right. Screw it.

739
00:57:02,304 --> 00:57:04,594
I know you're in there, Banner.
I'll get you out!

740
00:57:13,857 --> 00:57:15,857
What's the matter with you?
You're embarrassing me!

741
00:57:15,984 --> 00:57:17,194
I told them we were friends!

742
00:58:49,370 --> 00:58:51,450
Thunder! Thunder! Thunder!

743
00:58:53,249 --> 00:58:58,129
Thunder! Thunder! Thunder!

744
00:59:29,702 --> 00:59:32,412
Another day, another Doug.

745
00:59:41,297 --> 00:59:43,597
What is that noise?

746
00:59:43,758 --> 00:59:46,518
The common folk aren't exactly
falling in line.

747
00:59:46,677 --> 00:59:50,477
There's a resistance trying to knock down
the front gates.

748
00:59:56,020 --> 00:59:57,890
Tell me about yourself, Skurge.

749
00:59:58,064 --> 01:00:00,604
Well, me dad was a stonemason.
Me mum was...

750
01:00:00,775 --> 01:00:04,655
Right, yeah, I'll just stop you there.
What I meant was,

751
01:00:04,821 --> 01:00:06,441
what's your ambition?

752
01:00:07,573 --> 01:00:10,994
I just want a chance to prove myself.

753
01:00:11,578 --> 01:00:12,708
Recognition.

754
01:00:12,871 --> 01:00:14,241
When I was young,

755
01:00:14,414 --> 01:00:18,044
every great king had an executioner.

756
01:00:18,210 --> 01:00:20,260
Not just to execute people,

757
01:00:20,420 --> 01:00:23,000
but also to execute their vision.

758
01:00:24,049 --> 01:00:26,849
But mainly to execute people.

759
01:00:27,010 --> 01:00:29,010
Still, it was a great honor.

760
01:00:30,848 --> 01:00:33,648
I was Odin's executioner.

761
01:00:34,726 --> 01:00:38,986
And you shall be my executioner.

762
01:00:44,445 --> 01:00:46,445
Let's begin our conquest.

763
01:00:57,833 --> 01:00:59,453
Skurge, where's the sword?

764
01:01:04,923 --> 01:01:08,593
That sword is the key
to opening the Bifrost.

765
01:01:08,969 --> 01:01:12,559
Those people you mentioned,
the ones who aren't falling into line...

766
01:01:13,223 --> 01:01:14,433
Round them up.

767
01:01:38,123 --> 01:01:39,123
Excuse me.

768
01:01:51,637 --> 01:01:54,637
Sorry about that.
These bloody things are everywhere.

769
01:01:55,849 --> 01:01:56,939
Come on.

770
01:02:31,886 --> 01:02:33,556
You'll be safe here.

771
01:03:43,124 --> 01:03:44,124
Are we cool?

772
01:03:47,796 --> 01:03:49,466
It's Hulk in a hot tub.

773
01:03:50,757 --> 01:03:52,347
So how long
have you been like that?

774
01:03:52,759 --> 01:03:54,059
Like what?

775
01:03:54,803 --> 01:03:57,973
Like this. Big, and green, and stupid.

776
01:03:59,099 --> 01:04:01,269
Hulk always Hulk.

777
01:04:05,897 --> 01:04:07,317
How'd you get here?

778
01:04:08,108 --> 01:04:09,148
Winning.

779
01:04:09,943 --> 01:04:10,983
You mean cheating?

780
01:04:11,152 --> 01:04:13,362
Were they wearing one of these
when you won?

781
01:04:13,530 --> 01:04:14,830
How'd you arrive here?

782
01:04:17,867 --> 01:04:18,907
Quinjet.

783
01:04:18,993 --> 01:04:21,573
Yes. Now, where is the Quinjet now?

784
01:04:26,292 --> 01:04:28,292
That's naked.

785
01:04:28,461 --> 01:04:30,172
He's very naked.

786
01:04:33,926 --> 01:04:36,096
It's in my brain now.

787
01:04:36,720 --> 01:04:37,970
Quinjet.

788
01:04:48,441 --> 01:04:49,821
Yes!

789
01:04:49,984 --> 01:04:51,484
I'm getting us out of here.

790
01:04:51,652 --> 01:04:54,062
This terrible, awful place.

791
01:04:54,238 --> 01:04:57,948
You're gonna love Asgard.
It's big. It's golden. Shiny.

792
01:04:58,117 --> 01:04:59,497
Hulk stay.

793
01:04:59,660 --> 01:05:03,080
No, no, no. My people need me
to get back to Asgard.

794
01:05:03,789 --> 01:05:05,589
We must prevent Ragnarok.

795
01:05:05,749 --> 01:05:06,919
Ragnarok?

796
01:05:07,084 --> 01:05:10,464
The prophesied death of my home world.
The end of days, it's the end of...

797
01:05:12,506 --> 01:05:14,676
If you help me get back to Asgard,

798
01:05:14,842 --> 01:05:17,012
I can help you get back to Earth.

799
01:05:17,178 --> 01:05:18,178
Earth hate Hulk.

800
01:05:18,345 --> 01:05:19,925
Earth loves Hulk. They love you.

801
01:05:20,097 --> 01:05:22,807
You're one of the Avengers.
One of the team, one of our friends.

802
01:05:23,476 --> 01:05:25,370
This is what friends do.
They support each other.

803
01:05:25,394 --> 01:05:26,554
You're Banner's friend.

804
01:05:26,729 --> 01:05:28,939
I'm not Banner's friend. I prefer you.

805
01:05:29,106 --> 01:05:30,106
Banner's friend.

806
01:05:30,191 --> 01:05:31,241
I don't even like Banner.

807
01:05:31,317 --> 01:05:34,197
"I'm into numbers and science
and stuff."

808
01:05:34,612 --> 01:05:36,322
Thor go. Hulk stay.

809
01:05:36,489 --> 01:05:37,489
Fine.

810
01:05:38,199 --> 01:05:39,329
Stay here.

811
01:05:40,701 --> 01:05:42,411
Stupid place. It's hideous, by the way.

812
01:05:42,578 --> 01:05:46,038
The red, the white. Just pick a color.
Ridiculous.

813
01:05:46,832 --> 01:05:48,082
Smash you.

814
01:05:48,250 --> 01:05:50,550
You didn't smash anything.
I won that fight.

815
01:05:50,711 --> 01:05:52,841
- I smashed you.
- Yeah, sure, sure.

816
01:05:53,005 --> 01:05:54,755
- Baby arms.
- What?

817
01:05:54,924 --> 01:05:55,924
Baby.

818
01:05:56,175 --> 01:05:57,715
Moron! You big child.

819
01:05:57,885 --> 01:05:58,885
Thor go!

820
01:05:58,969 --> 01:06:00,219
I am going.

821
01:06:04,934 --> 01:06:06,394
Thor go again.

822
01:06:11,065 --> 01:06:12,355
Thor home.

823
01:06:22,493 --> 01:06:24,073
Hulk trains.

824
01:06:24,245 --> 01:06:26,325
That's great. Have fun.

825
01:06:26,497 --> 01:06:28,127
- Hey, big guy.
- Angry girl.

826
01:06:28,290 --> 01:06:29,590
What have you been up to?

827
01:06:29,750 --> 01:06:30,750
Winning.

828
01:06:41,138 --> 01:06:44,348
Heimdall, I know you can see me.

829
01:06:45,684 --> 01:06:47,684
I need you to help me.

830
01:06:49,813 --> 01:06:51,153
Help me see.

831
01:07:01,324 --> 01:07:03,824
I see you, but you're far away.

832
01:07:04,744 --> 01:07:05,994
What's going on here?

833
01:07:06,163 --> 01:07:07,543
Come see for yourself.

834
01:07:10,250 --> 01:07:13,050
I'm providing refuge in a stronghold
built by our ancestors.

835
01:07:13,211 --> 01:07:16,631
But if the garrison falls,
our only escape is Bifrost.

836
01:07:16,798 --> 01:07:18,838
You're talking about evacuating Asgard?

837
01:07:21,928 --> 01:07:24,058
We won't last long if we stay.

838
01:07:24,556 --> 01:07:27,226
She draws her power from Asgard
and grows stronger every day.

839
01:07:27,392 --> 01:07:28,522
Come on.

840
01:07:32,481 --> 01:07:33,981
Hela is ravenous.

841
01:07:34,149 --> 01:07:37,199
If I let her leave, she'll consume
Nine Realms and all the Cosmos.

842
01:07:37,402 --> 01:07:38,412
We need you.

843
01:07:38,570 --> 01:07:40,970
I'm working on it. But I don't even know
where the hell I am.

844
01:07:41,114 --> 01:07:43,395
You're on a planet surrounded
by doorways. Go through one.

845
01:07:43,450 --> 01:07:45,370
- Which one?
- The big one.

846
01:08:14,523 --> 01:08:15,823
Thor sad.

847
01:08:15,982 --> 01:08:17,192
Shut up.

848
01:08:19,444 --> 01:08:21,104
Thor sad.

849
01:08:22,155 --> 01:08:23,945
I'm not sad, you idiot.

850
01:08:24,366 --> 01:08:25,616
I'm pissed off!

851
01:08:27,077 --> 01:08:29,707
Angry. I lost my father.

852
01:08:30,872 --> 01:08:32,172
I lost my hammer.

853
01:08:33,333 --> 01:08:36,203
- Whining and crying. Cry like baby.
- You're not even listening.

854
01:08:36,628 --> 01:08:38,208
Don't kick stuff.

855
01:08:39,506 --> 01:08:41,676
You're being a really bad friend.

856
01:08:41,842 --> 01:08:43,052
You bad friend!

857
01:08:43,218 --> 01:08:44,538
- You know what we call you?
- No.

858
01:08:44,594 --> 01:08:46,384
We call you the stupid Avenger.

859
01:08:46,555 --> 01:08:48,476
You're tiny Avenger!

860
01:08:51,185 --> 01:08:52,345
What, are you crazy?

861
01:08:52,520 --> 01:08:53,520
Yes.

862
01:08:53,604 --> 01:08:56,144
You know what? Earth does hate you.

863
01:09:16,752 --> 01:09:17,802
No.

864
01:09:21,215 --> 01:09:23,885
I'm sorry I said those things.

865
01:09:24,635 --> 01:09:28,265
You're not the stupid Avenger.
Nobody calls you the stupid Avenger.

866
01:09:28,848 --> 01:09:30,308
It's okay.

867
01:09:30,475 --> 01:09:33,036
You just can't go around throwing shields
at people. Could have killed me.

868
01:09:33,060 --> 01:09:35,770
I know. I'm sorry.
I just get so angry all the time.

869
01:09:35,938 --> 01:09:38,068
Hulk always, always angry.

870
01:09:38,232 --> 01:09:40,572
I know.
We're the same, you and I.

871
01:09:41,068 --> 01:09:42,668
We're just a couple of hot-headed fools.

872
01:09:42,820 --> 01:09:46,780
Yeah, same.
Hulk like fire, Thor like water.

873
01:09:47,700 --> 01:09:49,410
We're kind of both like fire.

874
01:09:49,577 --> 01:09:51,577
But Hulk like real fire.

875
01:09:52,622 --> 01:09:54,962
Hulk like raging fire.

876
01:09:55,124 --> 01:09:57,374
Thor like smoldering fire.

877
01:09:59,879 --> 01:10:01,719
Hulk, I need you to do something for me.

878
01:10:08,304 --> 01:10:09,804
Angry girl.

879
01:10:17,146 --> 01:10:19,396
What's going on? What are you...

880
01:10:28,449 --> 01:10:30,289
You're so thick-headed
that you can't tell

881
01:10:30,451 --> 01:10:33,430
when someone's hiding all the way across
the universe and wants to be left alone?

882
01:10:33,454 --> 01:10:36,074
- We need to talk.
- No, you wanna talk to me.

883
01:10:36,833 --> 01:10:37,883
I need her to stay.

884
01:10:38,042 --> 01:10:39,042
Stay?

885
01:10:39,669 --> 01:10:40,799
Block.

886
01:10:42,463 --> 01:10:43,473
Stay.

887
01:10:44,173 --> 01:10:46,013
- Please.
- Please.

888
01:10:48,886 --> 01:10:49,886
All right.

889
01:10:51,889 --> 01:10:53,729
Here's the deal.

890
01:10:54,308 --> 01:10:56,018
I'll listen to you

891
01:10:56,728 --> 01:10:58,098
till this is empty.

892
01:10:59,565 --> 01:11:01,825
Asgard is in danger and
people are dying.

893
01:11:01,984 --> 01:11:03,704
We need to get back there.
I need your help.

894
01:11:05,612 --> 01:11:07,532
Finished. Bye.

895
01:11:09,158 --> 01:11:10,528
Odin is dead.

896
01:11:13,912 --> 01:11:16,162
Hela, the Goddess of Death,
has invaded Asgard.

897
01:11:16,957 --> 01:11:19,537
If Hela's back,
then Asgard's already lost.

898
01:11:19,710 --> 01:11:21,210
I'm going to stop her.

899
01:11:21,962 --> 01:11:23,052
- Alone?
- Nope.

900
01:11:23,213 --> 01:11:24,593
I'm putting together a team.

901
01:11:24,756 --> 01:11:27,506
It's me, you, and the big guy.

902
01:11:27,885 --> 01:11:30,105
No. No team. Only Hulk.

903
01:11:30,262 --> 01:11:31,932
It's me and you.

904
01:11:32,097 --> 01:11:33,217
I think it's only you.

905
01:11:33,390 --> 01:11:35,600
Please, listen.
The Valkyrie are legend.

906
01:11:35,768 --> 01:11:38,228
Elite warriors of Asgard
sworn to defend the throne.

907
01:11:38,979 --> 01:11:41,659
I'm not getting dragged into
another one of Odin's family squabbles.

908
01:11:41,815 --> 01:11:43,615
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Your sister.

909
01:11:43,734 --> 01:11:45,654
Her power comes from Asgard,
same as yours.

910
01:11:45,819 --> 01:11:48,465
When it grew beyond Odin's control
she massacred everyone in the palace

911
01:11:48,489 --> 01:11:49,989
and tried to seize the throne.

912
01:11:50,407 --> 01:11:52,117
When she tried
to escape her banishment

913
01:11:52,284 --> 01:11:54,664
he sent the Valkyrie in
to fight her back.

914
01:11:55,829 --> 01:11:57,959
I only survived because...

915
01:11:59,541 --> 01:12:02,921
Look, I already faced her once
back when I believed in the throne,

916
01:12:03,086 --> 01:12:04,336
and it cost me everything.

917
01:12:04,713 --> 01:12:06,463
That's what's wrong with Asgard.

918
01:12:06,632 --> 01:12:08,682
The throne, the secrets,
the whole golden sham.

919
01:12:08,842 --> 01:12:10,142
I agree.

920
01:12:11,053 --> 01:12:12,473
Don't get familiar.

921
01:12:12,930 --> 01:12:14,310
I agree.

922
01:12:14,473 --> 01:12:15,973
That's why I turned down the throne.

923
01:12:16,141 --> 01:12:19,271
But this isn't about the crown.
This is about the people.

924
01:12:19,436 --> 01:12:21,436
They're dying
and they're your people, too.

925
01:12:21,605 --> 01:12:22,605
Forget it.

926
01:12:23,899 --> 01:12:25,279
I have.

927
01:12:25,442 --> 01:12:26,652
- Okay.
- Okay.

928
01:12:26,819 --> 01:12:28,029
- Good. Great.
- Great.

929
01:12:28,195 --> 01:12:29,205
Thank you.

930
01:12:29,279 --> 01:12:30,949
- For what?
- For this.

931
01:12:33,283 --> 01:12:34,493
Didn't see that, did you?

932
01:12:35,994 --> 01:12:38,124
There... That's better.

933
01:12:39,873 --> 01:12:41,633
You know, go ahead.

934
01:12:41,792 --> 01:12:46,302
Stay here and enslave people
for that lunatic.

935
01:12:46,463 --> 01:12:47,843
Keep drinking, keep hiding.

936
01:12:48,006 --> 01:12:49,216
But me...

937
01:12:51,301 --> 01:12:54,431
I choose to run toward my problems
and not away from them.

938
01:12:55,514 --> 01:12:56,774
Because that's what...

939
01:13:01,812 --> 01:13:03,942
Because that's what heroes do.

940
01:13:15,410 --> 01:13:16,830
Friend stay!

941
01:13:28,840 --> 01:13:30,170
Yes!

942
01:13:44,814 --> 01:13:45,814
All right.

943
01:13:49,694 --> 01:13:50,694
Come on.

944
01:13:53,156 --> 01:13:55,576
Welcome. Voice activation required.

945
01:13:55,742 --> 01:13:56,912
Thor.

946
01:13:57,327 --> 01:13:58,537
Access denied.

947
01:13:59,871 --> 01:14:01,411
Thor, son of Odin.

948
01:14:01,581 --> 01:14:02,661
Access denied.

949
01:14:02,832 --> 01:14:03,872
God of Thunder.

950
01:14:04,042 --> 01:14:05,292
Access denied.

951
01:14:05,460 --> 01:14:06,580
Strongest Avenger.

952
01:14:06,753 --> 01:14:08,093
Access denied.

953
01:14:08,254 --> 01:14:09,804
Strongest Avenger.

954
01:14:09,964 --> 01:14:11,424
Access denied.

955
01:14:12,258 --> 01:14:13,718
Damn you, Stark.

956
01:14:14,135 --> 01:14:15,265
Point Break.

957
01:14:15,428 --> 01:14:17,638
Welcome, Point Break.

958
01:14:19,808 --> 01:14:21,178
Friend stay!

959
01:14:21,351 --> 01:14:22,351
No, no, no!

960
01:14:22,435 --> 01:14:23,485
Stop!

961
01:14:23,561 --> 01:14:24,561
Stay!

962
01:14:25,480 --> 01:14:26,860
Hulk, stop breaking everything!

963
01:14:27,023 --> 01:14:28,523
Don't go!

964
01:14:31,820 --> 01:14:33,110
Nice work, big guy.

965
01:14:33,279 --> 01:14:36,739
We don't know where Ultron's headed,
but you're going very high, very fast.

966
01:14:36,908 --> 01:14:38,708
So, I need you to turn this bird around,
okay?

967
01:14:39,327 --> 01:14:41,867
We can't track you in stealth mode,

968
01:14:42,038 --> 01:14:43,748
so I need you to help me out. Okay?

969
01:14:47,418 --> 01:14:48,958
I need you to...

970
01:15:05,186 --> 01:15:07,686
No! No, Banner!

971
01:15:14,863 --> 01:15:16,204
Oh, jeez.

972
01:15:17,116 --> 01:15:18,576
Banner.

973
01:15:19,743 --> 01:15:21,283
Hey, hey, hey.

974
01:15:21,454 --> 01:15:23,044
You all right, Banner?

975
01:15:25,458 --> 01:15:27,328
Sun's going down. Sun's going down.

976
01:15:27,751 --> 01:15:29,171
That's it, breathe.

977
01:15:30,379 --> 01:15:31,799
I won't hurt you.

978
01:15:32,381 --> 01:15:33,461
Sun's going down.

979
01:15:33,632 --> 01:15:35,052
- Thor.
- Yeah.

980
01:15:35,885 --> 01:15:37,265
What happened to your hair?

981
01:15:37,428 --> 01:15:38,758
Some creepy old man cut it off.

982
01:15:38,929 --> 01:15:40,389
- It looks good.
- Thanks.

983
01:15:40,556 --> 01:15:42,896
Where are we? How's Nat?

984
01:15:43,768 --> 01:15:46,018
- Nat is good, I'm sure.
- Is she okay?

985
01:15:46,228 --> 01:15:47,978
- And what about Sokovia?
- Sokovia?

986
01:15:48,147 --> 01:15:49,657
The city, Sokovia. Did we save it?

987
01:15:49,815 --> 01:15:50,985
- Banner, listen.
- What?

988
01:15:51,150 --> 01:15:53,150
Sokovia. Ultron. That was two years ago.

989
01:15:53,319 --> 01:15:54,819
What are you saying?

990
01:15:54,987 --> 01:15:56,107
What?

991
01:15:56,906 --> 01:15:58,326
I've been Hulk for two years?

992
01:15:58,657 --> 01:16:00,157
I'm afraid so.

993
01:16:06,123 --> 01:16:07,333
What the hell happened?

994
01:16:10,753 --> 01:16:12,423
Banner, there's something
you should know.

995
01:16:14,799 --> 01:16:15,879
Voice activation required.

996
01:16:16,050 --> 01:16:17,050
Banner.

997
01:16:17,218 --> 01:16:18,758
Welcome, strongest Avenger.

998
01:16:18,928 --> 01:16:19,928
What?

999
01:16:20,012 --> 01:16:21,052
Ship's log.

1000
01:16:32,483 --> 01:16:34,073
Thor, where are we?

1001
01:16:34,235 --> 01:16:35,285
Yeah, about that.

1002
01:16:35,444 --> 01:16:38,574
Sakaar, hear ye.
Attention please. I have some bad news.

1003
01:16:38,739 --> 01:16:41,529
My beloved exalted champion
has turned up missing.

1004
01:16:41,700 --> 01:16:44,120
Take to the streets.
Celebrate my champion.

1005
01:16:44,286 --> 01:16:45,296
Who's that?

1006
01:16:45,371 --> 01:16:47,001
He kind of runs the place.

1007
01:16:47,706 --> 01:16:49,184
You actually lived at his house
for awhile.

1008
01:16:49,208 --> 01:16:50,248
- I did?
- Yeah.

1009
01:16:50,417 --> 01:16:52,577
Quite a lot's happened.
You and I had a fight recently.

1010
01:16:53,045 --> 01:16:54,925
- Did I win?
- No, I won. Easily.

1011
01:16:55,089 --> 01:16:56,089
Doesn't sound right.

1012
01:16:56,173 --> 01:16:57,213
Well, it's true.

1013
01:16:57,299 --> 01:17:01,969
It seems that that criminally seductive
Lord of Thunder has stolen him away.

1014
01:17:02,138 --> 01:17:04,638
Seductive God of Thunder.
We need to move.

1015
01:17:05,391 --> 01:17:06,391
Oh, no.

1016
01:17:08,269 --> 01:17:09,389
This is bad.

1017
01:17:09,562 --> 01:17:11,602
This is really, really bad.

1018
01:17:14,316 --> 01:17:18,036
Thor, I think I'm freaking out.

1019
01:17:18,487 --> 01:17:19,487
No, no, no.

1020
01:17:19,572 --> 01:17:21,492
Don't freak out. You're okay.
Put these on.

1021
01:17:21,657 --> 01:17:22,697
These are Tony's clothes.

1022
01:17:22,867 --> 01:17:24,167
- I know, come on.
- Is he here?

1023
01:17:24,326 --> 01:17:26,347
No, he's not here.
But listen. Just stay calm, okay?

1024
01:17:26,371 --> 01:17:29,751
The sun's going down. The sun's getting
really low. Sun's going down.

1025
01:17:37,340 --> 01:17:39,210
I'm upset!

1026
01:17:42,220 --> 01:17:44,090
I'm very upset.

1027
01:17:44,264 --> 01:17:46,354
You know what I like about being upset?
The blame.

1028
01:17:46,516 --> 01:17:49,896
Right now, that's the mindset that I'm in.
And you know who I'm blaming?

1029
01:17:50,061 --> 01:17:51,601
- Grandmaster, I can...
- Hey!

1030
01:17:51,772 --> 01:17:52,812
Don't interrupt me!

1031
01:17:52,898 --> 01:17:53,988
Here you go.

1032
01:17:54,691 --> 01:17:56,171
Why are you handing me
the melt stick?

1033
01:17:56,276 --> 01:17:58,116
He was interrupting.

1034
01:17:58,278 --> 01:18:00,028
That's not a capital violation.

1035
01:18:00,197 --> 01:18:01,577
Where was I?

1036
01:18:01,948 --> 01:18:04,408
My precious champion
has come up missing,

1037
01:18:04,576 --> 01:18:07,836
and it's all because of that
Lord of Thunder. It's all because of him.

1038
01:18:07,996 --> 01:18:08,996
Your brother.

1039
01:18:09,080 --> 01:18:12,000
Whatever the story is.
Adopted, or complicated, or you know.

1040
01:18:12,167 --> 01:18:13,311
I'm sure there's a big history.

1041
01:18:13,335 --> 01:18:14,505
And your contender...

1042
01:18:15,295 --> 01:18:16,295
My dear friend,

1043
01:18:16,463 --> 01:18:19,753
if you were to give me 12 hours, I could
bring them both back to you. Alive.

1044
01:18:19,925 --> 01:18:21,425
I could do it in two.

1045
01:18:22,302 --> 01:18:23,382
I could do it in one.

1046
01:18:23,553 --> 01:18:24,593
Let's stop there.

1047
01:18:24,763 --> 01:18:28,433
You know what? I woke up this morning
thinking about a public execution.

1048
01:18:29,309 --> 01:18:30,661
But for now,
I'll settle for this sweet little

1049
01:18:30,685 --> 01:18:33,485
"Who's gonna get him first?"

1050
01:18:34,731 --> 01:18:37,061
So, you're on the clock.

1051
01:18:38,985 --> 01:18:40,075
What have you done?

1052
01:18:40,237 --> 01:18:41,487
I don't answer to you, lackey.

1053
01:18:41,655 --> 01:18:42,655
It's Loki.

1054
01:18:42,739 --> 01:18:44,399
And you will answer to the Grandmaster.

1055
01:18:47,494 --> 01:18:50,414
Why would you help my brother escape
with that green fool?

1056
01:18:50,580 --> 01:18:51,950
I don't help anyone.

1057
01:18:58,463 --> 01:18:59,593
You're a Valkyrie.

1058
01:19:04,511 --> 01:19:06,721
I thought the Valkyrie had all died
gruesome deaths.

1059
01:19:07,889 --> 01:19:09,599
Choose your next words wisely.

1060
01:19:09,766 --> 01:19:13,066
I'm terribly sorry.
Must be a very painful memory.

1061
01:20:05,698 --> 01:20:08,288
The sun's going down.
It's getting really low.

1062
01:20:09,452 --> 01:20:11,096
The sun's going down.
It's getting real low.

1063
01:20:11,120 --> 01:20:12,370
Oh, shoot.

1064
01:20:12,538 --> 01:20:14,668
- Sun's getting low.
- Would you stop saying that?

1065
01:20:14,832 --> 01:20:16,002
I just need you to stay calm.

1066
01:20:16,167 --> 01:20:18,087
Calm? I'm on an alien planet!

1067
01:20:18,252 --> 01:20:20,147
It's just a planet.
You've been on a planet before.

1068
01:20:20,171 --> 01:20:21,211
Yeah. One.

1069
01:20:21,380 --> 01:20:23,100
Now you've been on two.
That's a good thing.

1070
01:20:23,174 --> 01:20:24,384
It's a new experience.

1071
01:20:24,550 --> 01:20:28,630
My neurons, they're firing faster
than my brain can handle the information.

1072
01:20:28,805 --> 01:20:31,055
The whole thing
is totally different this time.

1073
01:20:31,224 --> 01:20:34,514
In the past, I always felt like Hulk
and I each had a hand on the wheel.

1074
01:20:34,685 --> 01:20:38,105
But this time, it's like he had the keys
to the car and I was locked in the trunk.

1075
01:20:38,272 --> 01:20:40,250
All right, well, you're back now.
That's all that matters.

1076
01:20:40,274 --> 01:20:41,354
No, it's not what matters.

1077
01:20:41,526 --> 01:20:44,276
What I'm trying to tell you, is that
if I turn into the Hulk again,

1078
01:20:44,445 --> 01:20:45,945
Banner may never come back.

1079
01:20:46,114 --> 01:20:49,404
And we're stranded on a planet
that is designed to stress me out.

1080
01:20:49,575 --> 01:20:52,125
We're not stranded. I'm gonna figure out
a way to get us home.

1081
01:20:52,578 --> 01:20:53,588
Thank you.

1082
01:20:53,663 --> 01:20:55,873
Not your home, though. Asgard.
My home.

1083
01:20:56,040 --> 01:20:57,080
What?

1084
01:20:57,250 --> 01:20:59,040
Listen, my people are in great danger.

1085
01:20:59,460 --> 01:21:01,710
You and I, we have to fight
this really powerful being,

1086
01:21:01,879 --> 01:21:03,709
who also happens to be my sister.

1087
01:21:03,881 --> 01:21:05,591
Okay, that is so wrong on so many...

1088
01:21:05,758 --> 01:21:08,268
I don't wanna fight your sister.
That's a family issue.

1089
01:21:08,427 --> 01:21:09,807
No, she's an evil being.

1090
01:21:09,971 --> 01:21:11,341
I don't care what she is.

1091
01:21:11,514 --> 01:21:13,854
I'm not fighting any more beings.
I'm sick of it.

1092
01:21:14,016 --> 01:21:15,106
- What?
- I just told you.

1093
01:21:15,268 --> 01:21:18,068
If I turn into the Hulk,
I am never gonna come back again.

1094
01:21:18,229 --> 01:21:19,279
And you don't care.

1095
01:21:19,439 --> 01:21:21,239
No, no. I'm putting together the team.

1096
01:21:21,399 --> 01:21:22,739
The Hulk is the fire.

1097
01:21:22,900 --> 01:21:24,700
Wait, you're just using me
to get to the Hulk.

1098
01:21:24,819 --> 01:21:26,369
- What? No!
- It's gross.

1099
01:21:26,529 --> 01:21:28,329
You don't care about me.
You're not my friend.

1100
01:21:28,448 --> 01:21:31,538
No! I don't even like the Hulk.
He's all like...

1101
01:21:31,701 --> 01:21:33,201
"Smash, smash, smash."

1102
01:21:33,369 --> 01:21:34,569
I prefer you.

1103
01:21:35,621 --> 01:21:36,621
Thanks.

1104
01:21:37,123 --> 01:21:40,213
But if I'm being honest,
when it comes to fighting evil beings,

1105
01:21:40,376 --> 01:21:41,796
he is very powerful and useful.

1106
01:21:41,961 --> 01:21:43,922
Yeah, Banner's powerful and useful, too.

1107
01:21:44,089 --> 01:21:45,219
Is he though?

1108
01:21:45,382 --> 01:21:47,502
How many PhDs
does Hulk have? Zero.

1109
01:21:47,676 --> 01:21:49,596
How many PhDs does Banner have?
Seven.

1110
01:21:50,345 --> 01:21:52,345
Fine, you don't have to fight anyone.

1111
01:21:52,514 --> 01:21:54,474
But we're in danger here,
so we have to move.

1112
01:21:58,395 --> 01:21:59,555
What are you doing with that?

1113
01:21:59,646 --> 01:22:00,707
I need a disguise. I'm a fugitive.

1114
01:22:00,731 --> 01:22:02,561
- I need a disguise.
- You are the disguise.

1115
01:22:03,233 --> 01:22:04,943
- I'll be Tony Stark.
- What?

1116
01:22:05,110 --> 01:22:06,860
Yeah. Tony and the gypsy.

1117
01:22:07,029 --> 01:22:09,489
No, no, you're not Tony.
You're Bruce. Bruce Banner.

1118
01:22:09,656 --> 01:22:11,092
Then why did you dress me up
like Tony?

1119
01:22:11,116 --> 01:22:12,116
Because you were naked.

1120
01:22:12,284 --> 01:22:13,664
Okay, I'll give you that.

1121
01:22:14,328 --> 01:22:15,597
What are you doing?
Stop doing that!

1122
01:22:15,621 --> 01:22:17,081
Tony wears his pants super tight.

1123
01:22:17,247 --> 01:22:18,297
- Stop it!
- I'm sorry.

1124
01:22:18,373 --> 01:22:20,503
- Why are you being so weird?
- I don't know.

1125
01:22:20,667 --> 01:22:23,007
Maybe the fact that I was trapped
for two years

1126
01:22:23,170 --> 01:22:25,760
inside of a monster
made me a little weird.

1127
01:22:25,923 --> 01:22:27,593
Hey. It's okay.

1128
01:22:27,758 --> 01:22:30,138
You're good. Calm down. Come on.

1129
01:22:30,302 --> 01:22:31,762
Listen, we're gonna go to Asgard

1130
01:22:31,929 --> 01:22:34,449
and you're not gonna have to think about
the Hulk ever again. All right?

1131
01:22:34,473 --> 01:22:35,473
All right.

1132
01:22:43,273 --> 01:22:44,643
This is bad.

1133
01:22:48,695 --> 01:22:50,115
Banner! Banner!

1134
01:22:54,118 --> 01:22:55,248
Banner!

1135
01:23:08,966 --> 01:23:10,006
Banner!

1136
01:23:10,425 --> 01:23:11,635
Thor!

1137
01:23:23,188 --> 01:23:24,188
Hi.

1138
01:23:24,273 --> 01:23:25,273
Hi.

1139
01:23:25,357 --> 01:23:26,567
I was gonna do that.

1140
01:23:26,733 --> 01:23:28,023
Yeah, well, I did it first.

1141
01:23:28,193 --> 01:23:30,193
That's good. What are you doing here?

1142
01:23:31,071 --> 01:23:32,841
What are you doing here?
I thought you were leaving.

1143
01:23:32,865 --> 01:23:33,865
I got sidetracked.

1144
01:23:34,408 --> 01:23:35,578
What's with the...

1145
01:23:35,742 --> 01:23:36,992
It's my disguise.

1146
01:23:37,161 --> 01:23:38,241
But I can see your face.

1147
01:23:38,579 --> 01:23:40,339
Not when I do this, you can't.

1148
01:23:40,956 --> 01:23:44,416
Your hair looks nice. I like what you did
with it. Change it? Washed it maybe?

1149
01:23:50,382 --> 01:23:53,173
What are those things on her eyes?
Are those people that she's killed?

1150
01:23:53,344 --> 01:23:55,030
She's so beautiful and strong
and courageous.

1151
01:23:55,054 --> 01:23:56,054
Who is this guy?

1152
01:23:56,139 --> 01:23:57,189
- He's a friend.
- Who? Me?

1153
01:23:57,265 --> 01:23:58,745
- I'm Bruce.
- I feel like I know you.

1154
01:23:58,850 --> 01:24:01,060
I feel like I know you, too.

1155
01:24:05,440 --> 01:24:08,570
Look, I've spent years in a haze,
trying to forget my past.

1156
01:24:09,360 --> 01:24:13,080
Sakaar seemed like the best place
to drink and forget, and to die one day.

1157
01:24:13,239 --> 01:24:16,539
I was thinking that you drink too much,
and that probably was gonna kill you.

1158
01:24:16,701 --> 01:24:17,901
I don't plan to stop drinking.

1159
01:24:18,703 --> 01:24:20,123
But I don't wanna forget.

1160
01:24:20,288 --> 01:24:21,918
I can't turn away anymore,

1161
01:24:22,540 --> 01:24:24,340
so if I'm gonna die,

1162
01:24:24,501 --> 01:24:27,701
well, it may as well be driving my sword
through the heart of that murderous hag.

1163
01:24:27,837 --> 01:24:29,427
- Good.
- Yeah.

1164
01:24:29,589 --> 01:24:32,599
So, I'm saying
that I wanna be on the team.

1165
01:24:33,176 --> 01:24:34,426
Has it got a name?

1166
01:24:34,594 --> 01:24:37,384
Yeah, it's called the Revengers.

1167
01:24:37,555 --> 01:24:38,555
Revengers?

1168
01:24:38,723 --> 01:24:41,223
Because I'm getting revenge.
You're getting revenge.

1169
01:24:42,977 --> 01:24:44,317
Do you want revenge?

1170
01:24:44,979 --> 01:24:46,689
I'm undecided.

1171
01:24:46,856 --> 01:24:47,856
Okay.

1172
01:24:48,441 --> 01:24:50,271
Also, I've got a peace offering.

1173
01:24:53,530 --> 01:24:55,540
Surprise.

1174
01:25:02,455 --> 01:25:03,915
Just had to be sure.

1175
01:25:07,544 --> 01:25:08,714
Hello, Bruce.

1176
01:25:10,046 --> 01:25:13,136
So, last time I saw you,
you were trying to kill everybody.

1177
01:25:13,299 --> 01:25:14,509
Where are you at these days?

1178
01:25:14,968 --> 01:25:16,848
It varies from moment to moment.

1179
01:25:17,929 --> 01:25:19,479
Is that a Dragonfang?

1180
01:25:19,639 --> 01:25:20,729
It is.

1181
01:25:20,890 --> 01:25:22,060
My God.

1182
01:25:22,934 --> 01:25:25,104
This is the famed sword of the Valkyrie.

1183
01:25:25,186 --> 01:25:28,396
So, Sakaar and Asgard are about as far
apart as any two known systems.

1184
01:25:28,565 --> 01:25:31,195
Our best bet is a wormhole
just outside of city limits.

1185
01:25:31,359 --> 01:25:34,989
Refuel on Xandar, and
we can be back in Asgard in 18 months.

1186
01:25:35,155 --> 01:25:38,405
Nope. We are going through the big one.

1187
01:25:38,575 --> 01:25:39,695
The Devil's Anus?

1188
01:25:39,868 --> 01:25:40,998
Anus?

1189
01:25:41,161 --> 01:25:42,304
Wait, wait, wait. Whose anus?

1190
01:25:42,328 --> 01:25:44,348
For the record, I didn't know
it was called that when I picked it.

1191
01:25:44,372 --> 01:25:46,202
That looks like
a collapsing neutron star

1192
01:25:46,374 --> 01:25:48,834
inside of an Einstein-Rosen Bridge.

1193
01:25:49,002 --> 01:25:51,792
We need another ship.
That will tear mine to pieces.

1194
01:25:51,880 --> 01:25:52,982
She's right. We need one that can

1195
01:25:53,006 --> 01:25:54,942
withstand the geodetic strain
from the singularity.

1196
01:25:54,966 --> 01:25:56,716
And has an offline
power steering system

1197
01:25:56,885 --> 01:25:59,635
that could also function
without the on board computer.

1198
01:25:59,804 --> 01:26:02,885
And we need one with cup holders,
because we're gonna die. So, drinks!

1199
01:26:03,058 --> 01:26:04,978
Do I know you? I feel like I know you.

1200
01:26:05,144 --> 01:26:07,014
I feel like I know you, too. It's weird.

1201
01:26:07,188 --> 01:26:08,318
What do you say?

1202
01:26:08,481 --> 01:26:11,001
Uncharted metagalactic travel
through a volatile cosmic gateway.

1203
01:26:11,108 --> 01:26:12,318
Talk about an adventure.

1204
01:26:12,902 --> 01:26:14,572
- We need a ship.
- Need a ship.

1205
01:26:14,737 --> 01:26:16,965
There are one or two ships.
Absolute top of the line models...

1206
01:26:16,989 --> 01:26:18,449
I don't mean to impose...

1207
01:26:21,702 --> 01:26:23,412
But the Grandmaster
has a great many ships.

1208
01:26:23,996 --> 01:26:27,536
I may even have stolen the access codes
to his security system.

1209
01:26:27,708 --> 01:26:30,145
And suddenly you're overcome
with an urge to do the right thing.

1210
01:26:30,169 --> 01:26:31,209
Heavens, no.

1211
01:26:31,295 --> 01:26:32,939
I've run out of favor
with the Grandmaster,

1212
01:26:32,963 --> 01:26:34,923
and in exchange for codes
and access to a ship,

1213
01:26:35,090 --> 01:26:38,350
I'm asking for safe passage
through the Anus.

1214
01:26:38,511 --> 01:26:41,101
You're telling us that you can get us
access into the garage

1215
01:26:41,263 --> 01:26:43,013
without setting off any alarms?

1216
01:26:43,182 --> 01:26:44,852
Yes, brother. I can.

1217
01:26:45,017 --> 01:26:47,767
Okay, can I just... A quick FYI.

1218
01:26:47,937 --> 01:26:49,748
I was just talking to him
just a couple minutes ago

1219
01:26:49,772 --> 01:26:52,282
and he was totally ready
to kill any of us.

1220
01:26:52,441 --> 01:26:53,611
He did try to kill me.

1221
01:26:53,776 --> 01:26:55,606
Yes, me too. On many, many occasions.

1222
01:26:55,778 --> 01:26:57,378
There was one time
when we were children,

1223
01:26:57,530 --> 01:27:00,290
he transformed himself into a snake,
and he knows that I love snakes.

1224
01:27:00,449 --> 01:27:02,289
So, I went to pick up the snake
to admire it,

1225
01:27:02,451 --> 01:27:05,212
and he transformed back into himself
and he was like, "Yeah, it's me!"

1226
01:27:05,329 --> 01:27:08,339
And he stabbed me.
We were eight at the time.

1227
01:27:08,833 --> 01:27:09,913
If we're boosting a ship

1228
01:27:10,084 --> 01:27:11,812
we're gonna need to draw some guards
away from the palace.

1229
01:27:11,836 --> 01:27:13,256
Why not set the beast loose?

1230
01:27:13,337 --> 01:27:14,377
Shut up.

1231
01:27:14,547 --> 01:27:15,627
You guys have a beast?

1232
01:27:15,798 --> 01:27:18,178
No, there's no beast.
He's just being stupid.

1233
01:27:18,384 --> 01:27:19,884
We're going to start a revolution.

1234
01:27:20,386 --> 01:27:21,966
- Revolution?
- I'll explain later.

1235
01:27:22,138 --> 01:27:24,428
- Who's this guy again?
- I'll explain later.

1236
01:27:25,266 --> 01:27:28,726
Is that some sort of protoplasm,
all the stuff that's coming out of you,

1237
01:27:28,894 --> 01:27:30,184
or are they eggs?

1238
01:27:31,480 --> 01:27:32,730
Looks like eggs.

1239
01:27:42,116 --> 01:27:43,536
I'm looking for Korg.

1240
01:27:43,701 --> 01:27:45,001
Who's asking?

1241
01:27:45,161 --> 01:27:46,331
I know you're asking.

1242
01:27:46,495 --> 01:27:48,495
Is there anyone else asking,
or is it just you?

1243
01:27:48,664 --> 01:27:50,874
The Lord of Thunder sends his best.

1244
01:27:54,378 --> 01:27:56,468
The revolution has begun.

1245
01:27:56,714 --> 01:27:58,754
Revolution? How did this happen?

1246
01:27:58,924 --> 01:28:00,424
Don't know.

1247
01:28:00,593 --> 01:28:03,763
But the arena's mainframe for the
Obedience Disks have been deactivated

1248
01:28:03,929 --> 01:28:05,809
and the slaves have armed themselves.

1249
01:28:06,474 --> 01:28:08,054
I don't like that word.

1250
01:28:08,225 --> 01:28:09,515
Which? Mainframe?

1251
01:28:09,685 --> 01:28:11,766
No. Why would I not like "mainframe"?

1252
01:28:11,938 --> 01:28:13,978
No, the "S" word.

1253
01:28:14,149 --> 01:28:16,899
Sorry, the prisoners with jobs
have armed themselves.

1254
01:28:18,320 --> 01:28:19,660
Okay, that's better.

1255
01:28:25,660 --> 01:28:27,620
Hey, so, listen. We should talk.

1256
01:28:29,080 --> 01:28:30,130
I disagree.

1257
01:28:30,499 --> 01:28:33,419
Open communication
was never our family's forte.

1258
01:28:33,585 --> 01:28:34,705
You have no idea.

1259
01:28:34,878 --> 01:28:37,548
Been quite the revelation
since we last spoke.

1260
01:28:37,714 --> 01:28:38,714
Hello.

1261
01:28:39,549 --> 01:28:40,549
Hi.

1262
01:28:47,849 --> 01:28:49,479
Odin brought us together.

1263
01:28:50,268 --> 01:28:53,108
It's almost poetic that his death
should split us apart.

1264
01:28:59,152 --> 01:29:01,282
We might as well be strangers now.

1265
01:29:01,446 --> 01:29:04,616
Two sons of the crown, set adrift.

1266
01:29:07,619 --> 01:29:09,179
Thought you didn't wanna talk about it.

1267
01:29:10,747 --> 01:29:11,747
Here's the thing.

1268
01:29:11,915 --> 01:29:13,755
I'm probably better off staying here
on Sakaar.

1269
01:29:13,875 --> 01:29:15,585
That's exactly what I was thinking.

1270
01:29:17,462 --> 01:29:18,882
Did you just agree with me?

1271
01:29:19,047 --> 01:29:20,627
Come on, this place is perfect for you.

1272
01:29:20,799 --> 01:29:22,469
It's savage, chaotic, lawless...

1273
01:29:22,634 --> 01:29:24,294
Brother, you're gonna do great here.

1274
01:29:24,469 --> 01:29:26,179
Do you truly think so little of me?

1275
01:29:28,265 --> 01:29:30,015
Loki, I thought the world of you.

1276
01:29:31,101 --> 01:29:33,691
I thought we were gonna fight
side by side forever.

1277
01:29:33,854 --> 01:29:36,684
But at the end of the day,
you're you and I'm me.

1278
01:29:37,399 --> 01:29:39,859
I don't know,
maybe there's still good in you.

1279
01:29:40,026 --> 01:29:43,526
But let's be honest,
our paths diverged a long time ago.

1280
01:29:48,201 --> 01:29:49,251
Yeah.

1281
01:29:50,412 --> 01:29:52,852
It's probably for the best
that we never see each other again.

1282
01:29:52,956 --> 01:29:54,246
It's what you always wanted.

1283
01:29:58,462 --> 01:30:00,172
Hey, let's do "Get Help."

1284
01:30:00,338 --> 01:30:01,588
- What?
- "Get Help."

1285
01:30:01,673 --> 01:30:02,673
No.

1286
01:30:02,757 --> 01:30:03,860
- Come on, you love it.
- I hate it.

1287
01:30:03,884 --> 01:30:05,528
- It's great. It works every time.
- It's humiliating.

1288
01:30:05,552 --> 01:30:06,863
- Do you have a better plan?
- No.

1289
01:30:06,887 --> 01:30:07,887
We're doing it.

1290
01:30:08,054 --> 01:30:09,844
We are not doing "Get Help."

1291
01:30:10,891 --> 01:30:12,141
Get help! Please!

1292
01:30:12,309 --> 01:30:13,349
My brother, he's dying.

1293
01:30:13,518 --> 01:30:15,518
Get help! Help him!

1294
01:30:17,564 --> 01:30:18,814
Classic.

1295
01:30:19,191 --> 01:30:20,282
Still hate it.

1296
01:30:20,443 --> 01:30:22,783
- It's humiliating.
- Not for me, it's not.

1297
01:30:22,945 --> 01:30:25,065
Now, which one's the ship
she told us to get?

1298
01:30:25,239 --> 01:30:26,239
The Commodore.

1299
01:30:26,908 --> 01:30:27,908
Right.

1300
01:30:30,745 --> 01:30:33,325
Though I feel it won't make
much of a difference.

1301
01:30:35,458 --> 01:30:37,248
Loki.

1302
01:30:38,419 --> 01:30:39,897
I know I've betrayed you many times
before,

1303
01:30:39,921 --> 01:30:41,591
but this time
it's truly nothing personal.

1304
01:30:41,756 --> 01:30:44,836
The reward for your capture
will set me up nicely.

1305
01:30:45,009 --> 01:30:46,639
Never one for sentiment, were you?

1306
01:30:46,803 --> 01:30:48,263
Easier to let it burn.

1307
01:30:48,596 --> 01:30:49,596
I agree.

1308
01:30:58,064 --> 01:30:59,694
That looks painful.

1309
01:31:00,399 --> 01:31:03,239
Dear brother,
you're becoming predictable.

1310
01:31:03,402 --> 01:31:05,412
I trust you, you betray me.

1311
01:31:05,571 --> 01:31:07,621
Round and round in circles we go.

1312
01:31:07,782 --> 01:31:09,782
See, Loki, life is about...
It's about growth.

1313
01:31:09,951 --> 01:31:11,161
It's about change.

1314
01:31:11,327 --> 01:31:14,537
But you seem to
just wanna stay the same.

1315
01:31:15,081 --> 01:31:16,711
I guess what I'm trying to say

1316
01:31:16,874 --> 01:31:19,834
is that you'll always be
the God of Mischief,

1317
01:31:20,002 --> 01:31:21,502
but you could be more.

1318
01:31:23,965 --> 01:31:25,965
I'll just put this over here for you.

1319
01:31:26,134 --> 01:31:29,644
Anyway, all got places to be,
so good luck.

1320
01:31:35,476 --> 01:31:36,846
All right, I can figure this out.

1321
01:31:37,019 --> 01:31:38,979
It's just another spaceship.

1322
01:31:52,201 --> 01:31:53,581
Loyal Sakaarians,

1323
01:31:53,744 --> 01:31:57,284
Lord of Thunder has stolen my ship
and my favorite champion.

1324
01:31:58,708 --> 01:32:01,878
Sakaarians, take to the skies.
Bring him down.

1325
01:32:02,044 --> 01:32:03,834
Do not let him leave this planet.

1326
01:32:16,809 --> 01:32:18,269
- Good shot!
- Thanks.

1327
01:32:20,980 --> 01:32:22,190
Open the doors.

1328
01:32:22,356 --> 01:32:23,776
Okay.

1329
01:32:28,905 --> 01:32:30,776
I hope that you're tougher
than you look.

1330
01:32:30,949 --> 01:32:31,989
Why?

1331
01:32:44,463 --> 01:32:46,303
Shouldn't we be shooting back
or something?

1332
01:32:46,465 --> 01:32:47,515
Yes, we should.

1333
01:32:47,591 --> 01:32:49,471
Where are the guns on this ship?

1334
01:32:49,635 --> 01:32:51,015
There aren't any.

1335
01:32:51,178 --> 01:32:52,758
- It's a leisure vessel.
- What?

1336
01:32:52,930 --> 01:32:55,770
Grandmaster uses it for his good times,
orgies and stuff.

1337
01:32:55,933 --> 01:32:58,523
Did she just say the Grandmaster
uses it for orgies?

1338
01:32:58,685 --> 01:32:59,885
Yeah.

1339
01:33:00,062 --> 01:33:01,482
Don't touch anything.

1340
01:33:21,792 --> 01:33:22,792
No!

1341
01:33:26,088 --> 01:33:27,128
- No!
- No!

1342
01:33:34,096 --> 01:33:35,176
Get inside!

1343
01:33:35,347 --> 01:33:37,017
In a minute.

1344
01:33:48,360 --> 01:33:50,380
I should probably go and help.
Here, take the wheel.

1345
01:33:50,404 --> 01:33:52,004
No. I don't know
how to fly one of these.

1346
01:33:52,072 --> 01:33:53,782
You're a scientist.
Use one of your PhDs.

1347
01:33:53,949 --> 01:33:57,239
None of them are for flying
alien spaceships!

1348
01:34:31,653 --> 01:34:32,703
Okay, come on.

1349
01:34:32,780 --> 01:34:34,910
There's gotta be a gun on this thing.

1350
01:34:35,073 --> 01:34:36,123
That looks like a gun.

1351
01:34:37,242 --> 01:34:39,873
It's my birthday
It's my birthday

1352
01:34:40,622 --> 01:34:43,042
It's my birthday

1353
01:34:49,714 --> 01:34:51,014
Yeah!

1354
01:35:08,316 --> 01:35:10,566
Guys, we're coming up
on the Devil's Anus!

1355
01:35:17,325 --> 01:35:18,335
There she is.

1356
01:35:18,493 --> 01:35:20,543
Our ticket out of here.

1357
01:35:20,995 --> 01:35:22,295
Hey, what's this?

1358
01:35:27,335 --> 01:35:28,345
Thank you.

1359
01:35:28,419 --> 01:35:30,919
Hey, man. We're about to jump
on that ginormous spaceship.

1360
01:35:31,005 --> 01:35:32,015
You wanna come?

1361
01:35:32,507 --> 01:35:36,837
You do seem like you're
in desperate need of leadership.

1362
01:35:37,011 --> 01:35:38,551
Why, thank you.

1363
01:35:42,308 --> 01:35:43,388
Here we go.

1364
01:35:49,983 --> 01:35:50,983
Shit.

1365
01:36:08,418 --> 01:36:10,208
Asgardians...

1366
01:36:10,378 --> 01:36:12,958
Some misguided soul

1367
01:36:13,756 --> 01:36:15,716
has stolen the Bifrost sword.

1368
01:36:15,884 --> 01:36:18,264
Tell us where it is

1369
01:36:18,428 --> 01:36:21,048
or there will be consequences.

1370
01:36:24,976 --> 01:36:26,096
Bad ones.

1371
01:36:29,272 --> 01:36:30,272
Well?

1372
01:36:37,363 --> 01:36:38,533
You.

1373
01:37:14,610 --> 01:37:18,820
Well? Executioner?

1374
01:37:23,786 --> 01:37:24,996
Wait!

1375
01:37:25,162 --> 01:37:26,162
Wait!

1376
01:37:28,666 --> 01:37:29,796
I know where the sword is.

1377
01:38:12,710 --> 01:38:14,960
I never thought I'd be back here.

1378
01:38:18,549 --> 01:38:20,129
I thought it'd be a lot nicer.

1379
01:38:20,593 --> 01:38:23,593
I mean, not that it's not nice.
It's just, it's on fire.

1380
01:38:23,762 --> 01:38:25,002
Here, up here in the mountains.

1381
01:38:25,222 --> 01:38:27,392
Heat signatures.
People clustered together.

1382
01:38:27,600 --> 01:38:28,600
She's coming for them.

1383
01:38:28,767 --> 01:38:30,745
Okay, drop me off at the palace
and I'll draw her away.

1384
01:38:30,769 --> 01:38:32,019
And get yourself killed?

1385
01:38:32,188 --> 01:38:34,082
The people trapped down there
are all that matters.

1386
01:38:34,106 --> 01:38:36,877
While I'm dealing with Hela, I need you
two to help get everyone off Asgard.

1387
01:38:36,901 --> 01:38:38,691
How the hell are we supposed to do that?

1388
01:38:39,195 --> 01:38:40,825
I have a man on the ground.

1389
01:38:46,786 --> 01:38:47,786
Asgard.

1390
01:38:51,207 --> 01:38:52,547
She's here.

1391
01:39:04,095 --> 01:39:05,805
Now the ship has a gun.

1392
01:39:05,972 --> 01:39:07,142
I'll take it from here.

1393
01:39:07,974 --> 01:39:11,104
I found this in the armory.

1394
01:39:14,272 --> 01:39:15,482
Good luck.

1395
01:39:16,942 --> 01:39:18,362
Your Majesty...

1396
01:39:20,320 --> 01:39:21,440
Don't die.

1397
01:39:24,241 --> 01:39:26,031
You know what I mean.

1398
01:40:24,926 --> 01:40:26,846
We must keep moving!

1399
01:40:27,471 --> 01:40:29,261
Go to the Bifrost!

1400
01:41:11,849 --> 01:41:13,219
Sister.

1401
01:41:15,228 --> 01:41:17,028
You're still alive.

1402
01:41:17,188 --> 01:41:20,658
I love what you've done with the place.
Redecorating, I see.

1403
01:41:20,817 --> 01:41:25,367
It seems our father's solution
to every problem was to cover it up.

1404
01:41:27,031 --> 01:41:28,651
Or to cast it out.

1405
01:41:30,910 --> 01:41:34,410
He told you you were worthy.
He said the same thing to me.

1406
01:41:34,997 --> 01:41:36,377
You see?

1407
01:41:37,041 --> 01:41:39,161
You never knew him.

1408
01:41:39,460 --> 01:41:41,370
Not at his best.

1409
01:41:41,546 --> 01:41:46,096
Odin and I drowned entire civilizations
in blood and tears.

1410
01:41:46,259 --> 01:41:49,179
Where do you think all this gold
came from?

1411
01:41:49,345 --> 01:41:51,095
And then, one day,

1412
01:41:51,264 --> 01:41:54,264
he decided to become a benevolent king.

1413
01:41:54,433 --> 01:41:57,063
To foster peace, to protect life.

1414
01:41:58,187 --> 01:41:59,777
To have you.

1415
01:42:00,231 --> 01:42:02,601
I understand why you're angry.

1416
01:42:02,775 --> 01:42:06,695
And you are my sister, and technically
have a claim to the throne.

1417
01:42:06,863 --> 01:42:08,841
And believe me, I would love
for someone else to rule.

1418
01:42:08,865 --> 01:42:10,075
But it can't be you.

1419
01:42:10,241 --> 01:42:13,911
You're just the worst.

1420
01:42:15,371 --> 01:42:17,161
Okay, get up.

1421
01:42:17,331 --> 01:42:19,371
You're in my seat.

1422
01:42:20,334 --> 01:42:22,334
You know, Father once told me

1423
01:42:22,503 --> 01:42:25,043
that a wise king never seeks out war.

1424
01:42:25,214 --> 01:42:27,754
But must always be ready for it.

1425
01:42:59,874 --> 01:43:01,334
Go back!

1426
01:43:06,464 --> 01:43:07,794
Go!

1427
01:43:42,709 --> 01:43:45,299
To be honest, I expected more.

1428
01:43:48,298 --> 01:43:49,598
Heimdall!

1429
01:43:51,802 --> 01:43:53,552
The sword!

1430
01:43:58,058 --> 01:43:59,608
Here's the difference between us.

1431
01:43:59,768 --> 01:44:01,358
I'm Odin's firstborn,

1432
01:44:01,520 --> 01:44:03,940
the rightful heir, the savior of Asgard.

1433
01:44:04,106 --> 01:44:05,856
And you're nothing.

1434
01:44:16,118 --> 01:44:18,998
So simple,
even a blind man could see it.

1435
01:44:22,708 --> 01:44:24,968
Now you remind me of Dad.

1436
01:44:35,262 --> 01:44:37,012
The stupid dog won't die!

1437
01:44:58,827 --> 01:45:01,837
Everything's gonna be all right now.
I got this.

1438
01:45:02,039 --> 01:45:04,129
You wanted to know who I am?

1439
01:45:05,083 --> 01:45:06,713
What the hell are you talking about?

1440
01:45:06,877 --> 01:45:08,297
You'll see!

1441
01:45:56,970 --> 01:45:59,180
You see? No one's going anywhere.

1442
01:45:59,347 --> 01:46:00,727
I'll get that sword,

1443
01:46:00,890 --> 01:46:03,610
even if I have to kill every
single one of them to do it.

1444
01:46:30,253 --> 01:46:31,253
Hey, man.

1445
01:46:32,797 --> 01:46:34,217
I'm Korg. This is Miek.

1446
01:46:34,382 --> 01:46:37,022
We're gonna jump on that spaceship
and get out of here. Wanna come?

1447
01:46:46,561 --> 01:46:50,401
Your savior is here.

1448
01:46:57,614 --> 01:46:59,484
Did you miss me?

1449
01:46:59,657 --> 01:47:01,117
Everyone, on that ship now.

1450
01:47:05,497 --> 01:47:07,667
Welcome home. I saw you coming.

1451
01:47:07,832 --> 01:47:08,912
Of course you did.

1452
01:47:25,600 --> 01:47:27,900
It's a valiant effort,
but you never stood a chance.

1453
01:47:28,937 --> 01:47:29,977
You see...

1454
01:47:30,772 --> 01:47:33,692
I'm not a queen or a monster.

1455
01:47:35,569 --> 01:47:37,239
I'm the Goddess of Death.

1456
01:47:38,364 --> 01:47:40,734
What were you the god of, again?

1457
01:47:52,086 --> 01:47:53,966
Even when you had two eyes,

1458
01:47:54,672 --> 01:47:56,552
you'd see only half the picture.

1459
01:47:58,134 --> 01:48:01,134
She's too strong.
Without my hammer, I can't.

1460
01:48:02,221 --> 01:48:05,771
Are you Thor, the God of Hammers?

1461
01:48:08,811 --> 01:48:12,531
That hammer was to help you
control your power, to focus it.

1462
01:48:13,315 --> 01:48:15,105
It was never your source of strength.

1463
01:48:15,818 --> 01:48:18,158
It's too late.
She's already taken Asgard.

1464
01:48:19,196 --> 01:48:21,866
Asgard is not a place. Never was.

1465
01:48:23,117 --> 01:48:24,407
This could be Asgard.

1466
01:48:25,578 --> 01:48:27,668
Asgard is where our people stand.

1467
01:48:28,664 --> 01:48:33,454
Even now, right now,
those people need your help.

1468
01:48:41,177 --> 01:48:43,307
I'm not as strong as you.

1469
01:48:45,973 --> 01:48:47,013
No...

1470
01:48:48,434 --> 01:48:49,724
You're stronger.

1471
01:48:58,736 --> 01:49:00,116
Tell me, brother.

1472
01:49:00,279 --> 01:49:02,739
What were you the god of, again?

1473
01:51:18,084 --> 01:51:20,294
- You're late.
- You're missing an eye.

1474
01:51:20,462 --> 01:51:21,972
This isn't over.

1475
01:51:29,095 --> 01:51:30,805
I think we should disband the Revengers.

1476
01:51:32,390 --> 01:51:33,630
Hit her with a lightning blast.

1477
01:51:33,683 --> 01:51:36,120
I just hit her with the biggest lightning
blast in the history of lightning.

1478
01:51:36,144 --> 01:51:37,144
It did nothing.

1479
01:51:41,149 --> 01:51:43,779
We just need to hold her off
until everyone's on board.

1480
01:51:44,402 --> 01:51:45,862
It won't end there.

1481
01:51:46,029 --> 01:51:49,449
The longer Hela's on Asgard,
the more powerful she grows.

1482
01:51:49,616 --> 01:51:51,326
She'll hunt us down.

1483
01:51:51,493 --> 01:51:53,044
We need to stop her here and now.

1484
01:51:53,204 --> 01:51:54,414
So what do we do?

1485
01:51:55,164 --> 01:51:56,744
I'm not doing "Get Help."

1486
01:52:08,886 --> 01:52:12,176
Asgard's not a place, it's a people.

1487
01:52:14,308 --> 01:52:15,348
Loki,

1488
01:52:15,434 --> 01:52:17,394
this was never about stopping Ragnarok.

1489
01:52:17,562 --> 01:52:19,612
This was about causing Ragnarok.

1490
01:52:19,772 --> 01:52:21,402
Surtur's crown, the vault.

1491
01:52:22,984 --> 01:52:24,444
It's the only way.

1492
01:52:24,944 --> 01:52:26,404
Bold move, brother.

1493
01:52:27,697 --> 01:52:29,277
Even for me.

1494
01:52:32,493 --> 01:52:33,543
Shall we?

1495
01:52:34,662 --> 01:52:35,662
After you.

1496
01:53:01,189 --> 01:53:02,689
This is madness.

1497
01:53:16,287 --> 01:53:17,867
Go! Go, now!

1498
01:54:18,892 --> 01:54:20,352
For Asgard.

1499
01:54:34,616 --> 01:54:35,946
Hela!

1500
01:55:00,517 --> 01:55:04,647
With the Eternal Flame, you are reborn.

1501
01:55:16,200 --> 01:55:17,450
Hela, enough!

1502
01:55:21,121 --> 01:55:24,001
You want Asgard, it's yours.

1503
01:55:24,166 --> 01:55:27,586
Whatever game you're playing,
it won't work.

1504
01:55:27,753 --> 01:55:29,423
You can't defeat me.

1505
01:55:30,047 --> 01:55:31,377
No, I know.

1506
01:55:33,091 --> 01:55:34,131
But he can.

1507
01:55:38,430 --> 01:55:39,810
No.

1508
01:55:48,398 --> 01:55:51,818
Tremble before me, Asgard!

1509
01:55:51,985 --> 01:55:54,105
I am your reckoning!

1510
01:56:02,830 --> 01:56:04,370
The people are safe.

1511
01:56:04,998 --> 01:56:06,878
That's all that matters.

1512
01:56:08,710 --> 01:56:10,050
We're fulfilling the prophecy.

1513
01:56:10,546 --> 01:56:11,917
I hate this prophecy.

1514
01:56:12,090 --> 01:56:13,880
So do I, but we have no choice.

1515
01:56:14,050 --> 01:56:15,840
Surtur destroys Asgard,

1516
01:56:16,010 --> 01:56:18,350
he destroys Hela,
so that our people may live.

1517
01:56:18,513 --> 01:56:21,263
But we need to let him finish the job,
otherwise...

1518
01:56:23,101 --> 01:56:24,101
No!

1519
01:56:26,354 --> 01:56:28,404
Hulk, stop, you moron!

1520
01:56:37,490 --> 01:56:38,530
Hulk, stop.

1521
01:56:38,700 --> 01:56:41,740
Just for once in your life, don't smash.

1522
01:56:42,912 --> 01:56:44,622
Big monster!

1523
01:56:44,956 --> 01:56:46,246
Let's go!

1524
01:56:48,042 --> 01:56:49,042
Fine.

1525
01:57:13,109 --> 01:57:15,989
I am Asgard's doom!

1526
01:57:38,968 --> 01:57:41,048
The damage is not too bad.

1527
01:57:41,221 --> 01:57:43,221
As long as the foundations
are still strong,

1528
01:57:43,389 --> 01:57:45,019
we can rebuild this place.

1529
01:57:45,183 --> 01:57:47,393
It will become a haven

1530
01:57:47,560 --> 01:57:50,520
for all peoples and aliens
of the universe.

1531
01:57:57,570 --> 01:57:59,990
Now those foundations are gone. Sorry.

1532
01:58:14,879 --> 01:58:16,799
What have I done?

1533
01:58:17,966 --> 01:58:20,386
You saved us from extinction.

1534
01:58:20,552 --> 01:58:22,393
Asgard is not a place...

1535
01:58:23,889 --> 01:58:25,759
It's a people.

1536
01:58:54,837 --> 01:58:56,347
It suits you.

1537
01:58:59,091 --> 01:59:01,551
Maybe you're not so bad after all,
brother.

1538
01:59:02,303 --> 01:59:03,343
Maybe not.

1539
01:59:04,555 --> 01:59:05,725
Thank you.

1540
01:59:06,474 --> 01:59:08,974
If you were here,
I might even give you a hug.

1541
01:59:13,063 --> 01:59:14,313
I'm here.

1542
01:59:38,589 --> 01:59:39,919
Your throne.

1543
01:59:55,022 --> 01:59:58,362
So, King of Asgard.

1544
02:00:08,869 --> 02:00:09,989
Where to?

1545
02:00:11,122 --> 02:00:12,542
I'm not sure.

1546
02:00:12,915 --> 02:00:14,215
Any suggestions?

1547
02:00:16,836 --> 02:00:18,796
Miek, where are you from?

1548
02:00:18,963 --> 02:00:20,803
Miek's dead.

1549
02:00:20,965 --> 02:00:24,095
Yeah, no, I accidentally stomped on him
on the bridge.

1550
02:00:24,260 --> 02:00:26,930
I've just felt so guilty,
I've been carrying him around all day.

1551
02:00:29,473 --> 02:00:30,934
Miek, you're alive!

1552
02:00:31,101 --> 02:00:33,431
He's alive, guys.
What was your question again, bro?

1553
02:00:35,313 --> 02:00:36,443
Earth it is.

1554
02:02:53,327 --> 02:02:56,037
Do you really think it's a good idea
to go back to Earth?

1555
02:02:56,205 --> 02:02:59,505
Yes, of course. The people of Earth
love me. I'm very popular.

1556
02:03:00,084 --> 02:03:02,004
Let me rephrase that.

1557
02:03:02,170 --> 02:03:05,380
Do you really think it's a good idea
to bring me back to Earth?

1558
02:03:05,923 --> 02:03:07,963
Probably not, to be honest.

1559
02:03:08,134 --> 02:03:13,054
I wouldn't worry, brother. I feel like
everything's gonna work out fine.

1560
02:09:41,989 --> 02:09:42,989
Oh, boy.

1561
02:09:51,415 --> 02:09:55,545
I just gotta say, I'm proud of you all.

1562
02:09:55,711 --> 02:09:59,131
This revolution has been
a huge success. Yay, us!

1563
02:09:59,298 --> 02:10:01,758
Pat on the back.
Pat on the back.

1564
02:10:01,926 --> 02:10:04,306
Come on. No?

1565
02:10:04,553 --> 02:10:06,593
Me too.
'Cause I've been a big part of it.

1566
02:10:06,764 --> 02:10:09,554
Can't have a revolution
without somebody to overthrow.

1567
02:10:09,725 --> 02:10:11,765
So, you're welcome.

1568
02:10:11,936 --> 02:10:14,266
And it's a tie.

